INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_61',
  'A development team is creating a new application and wants to define its AWS infrastructure using Python code, leveraging familiar programming constructs and libraries. They need a tool that translates this code into deployable AWS CloudFormation templates. Which AWS tool should they choose?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation macros","AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK)","AWS Serverless Application Model (SAM)","AWS CloudFormation Custom Resources"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Cloud Development Kit - CDK) allows developers to define cloud infrastructure using familiar programming languages like Python, TypeScript, Java, etc. The CDK then synthesizes these definitions into AWS CloudFormation templates for deployment. Option A (AWS CloudFormation macros) are used to process templates before CloudFormation creates or updates resources, but they don''t involve defining infrastructure with general-purpose programming languages. Option C (AWS Serverless Application Model - SAM) is an extension of CloudFormation for serverless applications, primarily using YAML/JSON. Option D (AWS CloudFormation Custom Resources) allows extending CloudFormation''s capabilities with custom logic, but not for defining entire infrastructures in a high-level programming language.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_62',
  'A DevOps team is experiencing slow deployment times and a high blast radius when updates fail for their application, which is managed by a single, large AWS CloudFormation stack containing all resources. They want to improve deployment efficiency and reduce the impact of failures. What is the recommended architectural change?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement AWS CloudFormation Change Sets before every deployment.","Break down the monolithic stack into smaller, interconnected AWS CloudFormation Nested Stacks.","Migrate the application to use AWS Elastic Beanstalk for deployments.","Use AWS Systems Manager State Manager to manage resource configurations."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Break down the monolithic stack into smaller, interconnected AWS CloudFormation Nested Stacks) directly addresses the anti-pattern ap-2.1-001, which highlights that monolithic stacks have slow deployments and a large blast radius. Nested stacks improve deployment speed, limit the blast radius, and enhance modularity and team autonomy. Option A (Implement AWS CloudFormation Change Sets) is a good practice for previewing changes but does not solve the underlying issues of a monolithic stack. Option C (Migrate to AWS Elastic Beanstalk) is a platform-as-a-service solution that might simplify application deployment but doesn''t directly solve the CloudFormation monolithic stack issue. Option D (Use AWS Systems Manager State Manager) is for instance configuration management, not for managing the deployment of CloudFormation infrastructure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_63',
  'A DevOps engineer is about to update an AWS CloudFormation stack. Historically, unexpected resource replacements or deletions have occurred during updates. To prevent this, the engineer wants to explicitly review all proposed changes before they are applied. Which CloudFormation feature should be used?',
  'mcq',
  '["Enable CloudFormation Rollback Triggers.","Perform a CloudFormation Drift Detection scan.","Create and review an AWS CloudFormation Change Set.","Apply a CloudFormation Stack Policy to protect resources."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Create and review an AWS CloudFormation Change Set) is the correct approach to preview what changes will be made to a stack''s resources before an update is executed. This directly addresses anti-pattern ap-2.1-002 by ensuring visibility into modifications, additions, or deletions. Option A (Enable CloudFormation Rollback Triggers) helps recover from failed deployments but doesn''t prevent unintended changes from being initiated. Option B (Perform a CloudFormation Drift Detection scan) identifies existing deviations from the template, not proposed future changes. Option D (Apply a CloudFormation Stack Policy) restricts updates to specific resources but doesn''t provide a preview of all changes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

