  '["AWS CloudFormation StackSets","AWS CloudFormation Custom Resources","AWS CloudFormation Macros and Transforms","AWS CloudFormation Drift Detection"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS CloudFormation Macros and Transforms) allows you to extend the CloudFormation template language. Macros can perform custom processing on your templates, while transforms (like AWS SAM Transform) provide predefined extensions to simplify template authoring. Option A (AWS CloudFormation StackSets) is for multi-account/Region deployment. Option B (AWS CloudFormation Custom Resources) is for managing resources not natively supported. Option D (AWS CloudFormation Drift Detection) identifies configuration deviations from the template.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_68',
  'An organization wants to ensure that all AWS CloudFormation templates submitted for deployment adhere to specific security and tagging policies. They need an automated way to validate these policies against the templates before they are deployed. Which AWS service should they use?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Config","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS CloudFormation Guard","AWS Service Catalog"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS CloudFormation Guard) is a policy-as-code language that allows you to define rules to check your CloudFormation templates for compliance with organizational policies, such as security and tagging, prior to deployment. Option A (AWS Config) assesses resource compliance after they are deployed. Option B (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) enforces configuration on EC2 instances. Option D (AWS Service Catalog) provides a curated catalog of approved products, not policy validation for raw templates.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_69',
  'A company needs to provide its developers with a self-service portal to provision pre-approved AWS resources, such as specific Amazon EC2 instances or Amazon S3 buckets, ensuring that these resources are always configured according to corporate governance standards. Which AWS service enables this capability?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation","AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK)","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Service Catalog) allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. End users can then provision these services from the catalog, ensuring that all deployed resources adhere to predefined governance and compliance standards. Option A (AWS CloudFormation) is for provisioning infrastructure but doesn''t provide a self-service portal with pre-approved products. Option B (AWS Cloud Development Kit - CDK) is for defining infrastructure as code using programming languages. Option D (AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store) is for storing configuration data and secrets.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_70',
  'A DevOps engineer needs to deploy a consistent Amazon S3 bucket configuration, including specific policies and encryption settings, across 50 different AWS accounts in multiple AWS Regions. They want to manage this deployment from a central account with minimal manual effort. Which AWS CloudFormation feature is most suitable?',
  'mcq',
  '["Using AWS CloudFormation Nested Stacks for each account.","Manually deploying the CloudFormation template in each account and Region.","Utilizing AWS CloudFormation StackSets from a central management account.","Implementing AWS Service Catalog to allow account owners to provision the bucket."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Utilizing AWS CloudFormation StackSets from a central management account) is the most efficient and scalable solution for deploying CloudFormation stacks consistently across multiple AWS accounts and Regions. It allows for a single operation to manage deployments to many targets. Option A (Using AWS CloudFormation Nested Stacks) is for modularity within a single stack, not for multi-account/Region deployment. Option B (Manually deploying the CloudFormation template) is prone to errors and high operational overhead, which is an anti-pattern for large-scale environments. Option D (Implementing AWS Service Catalog) provides a self-service portal, but StackSets is specifically designed for the centralized deployment of infrastructure across accounts and Regions.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_71',
  'A DevOps team wants to use a policy-as-code tool to validate their AWS CloudFormation templates against internal security and cost optimization guidelines before deployment. They need to define custom rules to check for non-compliant resource properties. Which AWS service allows them to define and apply these rules?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Config conformance packs","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS CloudFormation Guard","AWS Service Catalog"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS CloudFormation Guard) is a policy-as-code language that enables you to define custom rules to validate your CloudFormation templates against specific organizational policies, such as security and cost optimization guidelines, before they are deployed. Option A (AWS Config conformance packs) are used to assess compliance of *deployed* resources against a set of rules. Option B (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) enforces desired configurations on *running instances*. Option D (AWS Service Catalog) is for providing a curated catalog of approved products, not for policy validation of raw templates.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_72',
  'An organization needs to provide a self-service portal for developers to provision standardized AWS environments. These environments must adhere to specific security and tagging policies. Which AWS service allows administrators to curate a catalog of approved products and control their provisioning?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation","AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK)","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Systems Manager Explorer"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Service Catalog) allows administrators to create and manage catalogs of approved IT services (products) that users can then provision. This ensures that all deployed resources conform to predefined security, tagging, and architectural standards. Option A (AWS CloudFormation) is the underlying IaC service but doesn''t provide the self-service catalog interface. Option B (AWS Cloud Development Kit - CDK) is for defining infrastructure as code using programming languages. Option D (AWS Systems Manager Explorer) is an operations dashboard for operational data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  29,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_73',
  'Which AWS CloudFormation feature is specifically designed to deploy and manage a common set of AWS resources across multiple AWS accounts and Regions from a single CloudFormation template?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation Nested Stacks","AWS CloudFormation Change Sets","AWS CloudFormation StackSets","AWS CloudFormation Custom Resources"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS CloudFormation StackSets) provides the capability to deploy a common CloudFormation template across multiple AWS accounts and Regions simultaneously, making it ideal for standardizing infrastructure across an organization. Option A (AWS CloudFormation Nested Stacks) are for modularizing templates within a single stack. Option B (AWS CloudFormation Change Sets) are for previewing changes to a single stack. Option D (AWS CloudFormation Custom Resources) extend CloudFormation''s capabilities to manage unsupported resource types.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_74',
  'A DevOps team manages hundreds of AWS CloudFormation stacks across multiple AWS accounts and Regions. They need a robust method to ensure that all newly deployed stacks adhere to strict internal security and compliance policies, such as disallowing public S3 buckets or unencrypted Amazon RDS instances, before any resources are provisioned. Which AWS service or feature should the team implement to enforce these policies at the template validation stage?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation Guard","AWS Config conformance packs","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Systems Manager State Manager"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS CloudFormation Guard, a policy-as-code language that allows developers to define rules to check CloudFormation templates for compliance before deployment. It can be integrated into CI/CD pipelines to prevent non-compliant infrastructure from being provisioned. Option B (incorrect) AWS Config conformance packs are used to check compliance of *already deployed* resources against a set of AWS Config rules, not to validate templates pre-deployment. Option C (incorrect) AWS Service Catalog helps standardize the deployment of approved products but does not inherently enforce policy checks on arbitrary CloudFormation templates at the validation stage; it relies on pre-approved templates. Option D (incorrect) AWS Systems Manager State Manager is for configuring and maintaining the desired state of EC2 instances and on-premises servers, not for validating CloudFormation templates.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  31,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_75',
  'A development team uses AWS CloudFormation to manage its application infrastructure. They are experiencing slow deployment times and difficulty managing dependencies for a large, complex application defined within a single CloudFormation stack. Updates often affect unrelated components, increasing the blast radius of changes. Which CloudFormation feature should the team adopt to improve deployment speed, reduce blast radius, and enhance modularity?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation nested stacks","AWS CloudFormation change sets","AWS CloudFormation drift detection","AWS CloudFormation custom resources"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CloudFormation nested stacks allow breaking down a large CloudFormation template into smaller, reusable templates. This improves modularity, reduces deployment times for individual components, and limits the blast radius of changes to specific nested stacks. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation change sets are used to preview the changes a stack update will make before applying them, which helps prevent unexpected modifications but does not address the issues of monolithic stack deployment speed or blast radius. Option C (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation drift detection identifies when a stack''s actual configuration deviates from its template, which is for post-deployment auditing, not for improving deployment architecture. Option D (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation custom resources allow extending CloudFormation''s capabilities to manage resources not natively supported, which is unrelated to improving monolithic stack management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_76',
  'A DevOps engineer is responsible for provisioning standardized development environments for multiple teams. Each environment consists of a VPC, subnets, security groups, and an Amazon EC2 instance with specific configurations. The engineer wants to provide a self-service portal where developers can provision these environments with minimal configuration, ensuring consistency and adherence to organizational standards. Which AWS service is best suited for this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Service Catalog","AWS CloudFormation StackSets","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. It enables users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need, ensuring consistent governance and compliance, which perfectly fits the requirement for a self-service portal for standardized environments. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation StackSets are used for deploying CloudFormation stacks across multiple accounts and Regions from a single template, which is for multi-account/Region deployments, not primarily for self-service provisioning by end-users. Option C (incorrect) AWS Systems Manager State Manager is used for configuring and maintaining the desired state of EC2 instances, not for providing a self-service portal for provisioning infrastructure. Option D (incorrect) AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate is a configuration management service for managing server configurations using Chef, which is legacy and not designed for self-service infrastructure provisioning.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_77',
  'A company needs to deploy a common set of baseline security and networking infrastructure, such as IAM roles, VPCs, and AWS Config rules, across 50 different AWS accounts in three different AWS Regions. The infrastructure must be managed centrally from a single administrative account. Which AWS CloudFormation feature is designed for this specific multi-account, multi-Region deployment and management scenario?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation StackSets","AWS CloudFormation nested stacks","AWS CloudFormation custom resources","AWS CloudFormation change sets"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CloudFormation StackSets enable you to provision CloudFormation stacks across multiple AWS accounts and Regions with a single operation. This is ideal for deploying common baseline infrastructure consistently across an organization''s AWS environment. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation nested stacks are used to modularize templates within a single account and Region, not for multi-account or multi-Region deployments. Option C (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation custom resources allow you to write custom provisioning logic for resources not natively supported by CloudFormation, which is unrelated to multi-account, multi-Region deployments. Option D (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation change sets are used to preview changes before applying a stack update, which is a safety mechanism for updates, not a deployment mechanism for multiple accounts/Regions.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_78',
  'A DevOps team uses AWS CloudFormation to manage their infrastructure. They recently discovered that several Amazon S3 buckets, which were initially created with private access, have been manually modified to be publicly accessible outside of CloudFormation. The team needs an automated way to identify these unauthorized configuration changes. Which CloudFormation feature can detect when a stack''s resources have been altered manually or outside of its template?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation drift detection","AWS CloudFormation change sets","AWS CloudFormation custom resources","AWS CloudFormation StackSets"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CloudFormation drift detection allows you to identify when the actual configuration of resources in a stack differs from their expected configuration in the stack''s CloudFormation template. This is precisely what is needed to find manually modified resources like the S3 buckets. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation change sets are used to preview proposed changes to a stack before applying an update, not to detect post-deployment manual changes. Option C (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation custom resources extend CloudFormation''s capabilities to manage unsupported resource types, which is unrelated to detecting configuration drift. Option D (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation StackSets are used for deploying stacks across multiple accounts and Regions, not for detecting configuration drift within existing stacks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_79',
  'A company is migrating its legacy application configuration management from on-premises Chef servers to AWS. They have a large fleet of Amazon EC2 instances that require consistent software installation, file management, and service startup configurations. The company wants to leverage a managed AWS service that supports Chef-based automation without managing the underlying Chef infrastructure. Which AWS service is designed for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Config conformance packs","AWS CloudFormation Guard"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate provides a fully managed Chef Automate server, allowing customers to use their existing Chef cookbooks and recipes to automate configuration management for EC2 instances without needing to operate the Chef server infrastructure themselves. Option B (incorrect) AWS Systems Manager State Manager is a configuration management service that enforces and maintains desired state using Systems Manager documents, not Chef recipes. While it can manage configurations, it''s not designed for direct Chef integration in a managed service context. Option C (incorrect) AWS Config conformance packs are used for auditing and reporting compliance of AWS resources, not for active configuration management of instances. Option D (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation Guard is a policy-as-code tool for validating CloudFormation templates, which is unrelated to instance configuration management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_80',
  'A DevOps team uses AWS CloudFormation to provision infrastructure. They need to integrate a third-party service that is not natively supported by CloudFormation as part of their stack deployments. This service requires custom API calls to provision and manage its resources. Which CloudFormation feature allows the team to extend CloudFormation''s capabilities to manage these unsupported resources?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation custom resources","AWS CloudFormation macros","AWS CloudFormation nested stacks","AWS CloudFormation change sets"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CloudFormation custom resources allow you to write custom provisioning logic, typically using AWS Lambda functions, to manage resources that are not natively supported by CloudFormation. This enables integration with third-party services or custom internal tools. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation macros allow you to process templates before CloudFormation processes them, enabling custom template transformations, but they are not for managing external resources directly. Option C (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation nested stacks are used for modularizing templates within CloudFormation, not for extending its capabilities to external services. Option D (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation change sets are used to preview changes before applying a stack update, which is a safety mechanism, not an extension for unsupported resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_81',
  'An organization is adopting AWS CDK for defining its infrastructure. They want to ensure that all CDK applications adhere to specific coding standards and architectural patterns, such as using specific naming conventions for resources or enforcing certain security configurations across all constructs. Which AWS CDK feature allows developers to define reusable, higher-level abstractions that encapsulate these best practices and enforce consistency?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CDK custom constructs","AWS CDK aspects","AWS CDK templates","AWS CDK pipelines"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CDK custom constructs allow developers to encapsulate common patterns and best practices into reusable, higher-level components. This enables teams to define their own abstractions that enforce organizational standards and simplify infrastructure definition for other developers. Option B (incorrect) AWS CDK aspects allow applying modifications or validations to constructs in a specific scope, which can be used for policy enforcement but is a different mechanism than defining reusable architectural patterns. Option C (incorrect) AWS CDK does not directly use ''templates'' in the same way CloudFormation does; it generates CloudFormation templates. The term ''templates'' here is a plausible distractor but not a CDK feature for defining reusable abstractions. Option D (incorrect) AWS CDK pipelines are used for defining CI/CD pipelines for CDK applications, which is related to deployment automation, not defining reusable infrastructure patterns.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_82',
  'A DevOps team is using AWS CloudFormation to manage a complex application that includes Amazon S3 buckets, Amazon EC2 instances, and Amazon RDS databases. They need to transform the template dynamically at deployment time, for example, to inject environment-specific parameters or to generate resource configurations based on input variables. Which CloudFormation feature allows for custom processing of templates before CloudFormation processes them?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation macros","AWS CloudFormation custom resources","AWS CloudFormation nested stacks","AWS CloudFormation change sets"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CloudFormation macros allow you to perform custom processing on templates before CloudFormation processes them. This enables advanced template transformations, such as generating resources dynamically, injecting boilerplate, or simplifying complex structures. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation custom resources are used to manage resources not natively supported by CloudFormation, not for transforming the template itself. Option C (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation nested stacks are used for modularizing templates into smaller, reusable components, not for dynamic template transformations. Option D (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation change sets are used to preview changes before applying a stack update, which is a safety mechanism, not a template transformation feature.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_83',
  'A company is developing a new application using the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK). The development team consists of engineers proficient in Python, TypeScript, and Java. They want to ensure that all team members can contribute to the infrastructure definition using their preferred programming language while maintaining a unified infrastructure-as-code approach. Which statement accurately describes AWS CDK''s support for programming languages?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CDK supports TypeScript, Python, Java, C#, and Go for defining infrastructure.","AWS CDK only supports TypeScript, requiring transpilation for other languages.","AWS CDK primarily supports Python, with experimental support for Java and TypeScript.","AWS CDK requires a specific proprietary language for infrastructure definition."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CDK officially supports multiple popular programming languages, including TypeScript, Python, Java, C#, and Go. This allows development teams to define their cloud infrastructure using familiar languages, fostering broader adoption and collaboration. Option B (incorrect) is false; AWS CDK provides native support for multiple languages, not just TypeScript with transpilation. Option C (incorrect) is false; AWS CDK has robust, official support for all listed languages, not just experimental support for some. Option D (incorrect) is false; AWS CDK leverages standard programming languages, not a proprietary language, which is one of its key benefits.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_84',
  'A large enterprise has a policy that all Amazon EC2 instances must be configured with a specific set of security agents and monitoring tools upon launch. Currently, administrators manually install these agents after an instance is provisioned, leading to inconsistencies and compliance gaps. The enterprise needs an automated, continuous method to ensure all EC2 instances maintain this desired configuration state. Which AWS service should be used to enforce and remediate configuration compliance across the EC2 fleet?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Config conformance packs","AWS CloudFormation drift detection","AWS Service Catalog"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS Systems Manager State Manager is designed to enforce and maintain the desired state of EC2 instances and on-premises servers. It can automatically apply configuration baselines, install software, and ensure continuous compliance, directly addressing the need to automate agent installation and prevent configuration drift. Option B (incorrect) AWS Config conformance packs are used to audit the compliance of AWS resources against a set of rules, providing reports but not actively enforcing or remediating configurations on instances. Option C (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation drift detection identifies when a stack''s resources deviate from its template, but it doesn''t actively manage the configuration *within* an EC2 instance. Option D (incorrect) AWS Service Catalog allows users to provision approved IT services, but it doesn''t continuously enforce configuration compliance on running instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_1',
  'hard'
);

