  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) AWS CDK Aspects allow you to apply modifications or validations to constructs in a specific scope within your CDK application. This is ideal for implementing cross-cutting concerns like security policies, ensuring that all relevant resources (e.g., S3 buckets) meet compliance requirements by traversing the construct tree and applying checks. Option B (incorrect) AWS CDK Custom Constructs are for encapsulating reusable patterns or integrating with external services, not primarily for applying policy checks across existing constructs. Option C (incorrect) AWS CDK Stacks are deployment units and do not inherently provide policy enforcement capabilities. Option D (incorrect) AWS CDK Pipelines are for defining CI/CD workflows for CDK applications, which is about deployment automation, not in-code policy enforcement.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  89,
