  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) states that a multi-Region architecture provides resilience against an entire AWS Region outage, which is a primary reason for adopting such a pattern. Option B (incorrect) is contrary to multi-Region design, which distributes data. Option C (incorrect) describes the benefit of deploying resources closer to users, which a multi-Region setup can achieve, but the key characteristic is resilience. Option D (incorrect) is false; load balancers are often crucial in multi-Region deployments.',
