  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the main benefit of Multi-AZ deployment. Availability Zones are physically isolated locations within an AWS Region, so deploying across multiple AZs protects applications from failures of a single data center. Option A describes multi-Region deployments or services like AWS Global Accelerator. Option C describes Auto Scaling groups. Option D requires a multi-Region architecture, as Multi-AZ protects against failures within a single region, not an entire regional outage.',
