  '["Amazon RDS Multi-AZ deployment","Amazon DynamoDB Global Tables","Amazon RDS cross-Region read replica","Amazon Aurora Global Database"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is Amazon Aurora Global Database. It is designed for globally distributed applications, allowing a single Aurora database to span multiple AWS Regions, with fast cross-Region replication for disaster recovery and low-latency global reads. Option A (Amazon RDS Multi-AZ) provides high availability within a single region. Option B (Amazon DynamoDB Global Tables) is a NoSQL database. Option C (Amazon RDS cross-Region read replica) provides read scalability and DR but is not as tightly integrated for global active-active as Aurora Global Database.',
