INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_67',
  'A large enterprise needs to deploy a standardized networking stack (VPC, subnets, route tables) across 50 different AWS accounts in multiple Regions. Which two AWS services or features can facilitate this large-scale, consistent deployment? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["CloudFormation StackSets","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS CDK","CloudFormation Guard"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (CloudFormation StackSets) is specifically designed for deploying CloudFormation stacks across multiple AWS accounts and Regions from a single template, ensuring consistency at scale. Option B (AWS Service Catalog) can be used to define the standardized networking stack as a product, allowing teams to self-provision it while adhering to central governance and consistency. Option C (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) is for configuration management of instances, not for deploying foundational infrastructure. Option D (AWS CDK) is a tool for defining IaC, but StackSets is the mechanism for multi-account deployment. Option E (CloudFormation Guard) is for policy checking.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_68',
  'To enable self-service provisioning of pre-approved infrastructure templates while maintaining governance, which two AWS services work together effectively? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Service Catalog","AWS CloudFormation","AWS Systems Manager Inventory","AWS Config","AWS OpsWorks"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Service Catalog) is designed to allow end-users to provision pre-approved IT services in a self-service manner. Option B (AWS CloudFormation) is the underlying service used to define these IT services (products) as templates within Service Catalog, ensuring they are standardized and repeatable. Option C (AWS Systems Manager Inventory) collects data about instances. Option D (AWS Config) assesses resource configurations for compliance. Option E (AWS OpsWorks) is a legacy configuration management service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_69',
  'A company wants to enforce security policies on its infrastructure definitions before deployment and continuously assess the compliance of deployed resources. Which two AWS services or features can achieve this policy-as-code approach? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["CloudFormation Guard","AWS Config conformance packs","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Service Catalog","AWS OpsWorks"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (CloudFormation Guard) allows you to define policies in code to validate CloudFormation templates against security and compliance rules *before* deployment. Option B (AWS Config conformance packs) provide a way to deploy and manage a collection of AWS Config rules and remediation actions as a single entity, continuously assessing the compliance of *deployed* resources. Option C (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) enforces configuration on instances. Option D (AWS Service Catalog) is for provisioning. Option E (AWS OpsWorks) is a legacy configuration management service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_70',
  'A company wants to ensure all newly launched EC2 instances automatically adhere to specific security hardening configurations and that any drift from this baseline is automatically corrected. Which two AWS Systems Manager capabilities are most suitable? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["State Manager","Patch Manager","Run Command","Session Manager","Parameter Store"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (State Manager) allows you to define and enforce a desired state for your EC2 instances, ensuring they adhere to security hardening configurations and automatically remediating any deviations. Option B (Patch Manager) is crucial for security hardening by ensuring instances receive the latest security updates. Option C (Run Command) executes commands on-demand, but doesn''t enforce continuous state. Option D (Session Manager) provides secure shell access. Option E (Parameter Store) stores configuration data, but doesn''t enforce it.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_71',
  'To prevent and detect configuration drift in an AWS environment, which two services or features are most effective? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS CloudFormation Drift Detection","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Service Catalog","AWS CDK","AWS OpsWorks"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS CloudFormation Drift Detection) is specifically designed to identify when the actual configuration of stack resources differs from their expected configuration in the CloudFormation template. Option B (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) helps prevent drift by continuously enforcing a desired configuration state on EC2 instances and other managed nodes. Option C (AWS Service Catalog) is for standardized provisioning, not drift management. Option D (AWS CDK) is an IaC tool, not a drift detection/prevention mechanism itself. Option E (AWS OpsWorks) is a legacy configuration management service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_72',
  'Which two AWS CloudFormation features promote reusability and modularity when defining infrastructure as code? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Nested Stacks","Custom Resources","Change Sets","StackSets","CloudFormation Guard"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (Nested Stacks) allow you to break down a large CloudFormation template into smaller, reusable components, promoting modularity. Option D (StackSets) enable you to deploy a common set of resources across multiple accounts and Regions from a single template, which inherently promotes reusability of infrastructure patterns. Option B (Custom Resources) extend CloudFormation''s capabilities but are not primarily for reusability of templates. Option C (Change Sets) are for previewing changes. Option E (CloudFormation Guard) is for policy checking.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_73',
  'A company needs to manage the compliance of its EC2 instance fleet by collecting software inventory and ensuring specific configurations are applied. Which two AWS services can help achieve this? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Inventory","AWS Config","AWS CloudFormation","AWS Service Catalog","AWS OpsWorks"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Systems Manager Inventory) automatically collects data about your EC2 instances, including installed applications, configurations, and network settings. Option B (AWS Config) can be used to define rules to assess and ensure that the collected configurations comply with desired standards. Option C (AWS CloudFormation) is for defining infrastructure, not for managing the configuration of running instances. Option D (AWS Service Catalog) is for provisioning. Option E (AWS OpsWorks) is a legacy configuration management service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_74',
  'Before deploying a CloudFormation stack update, a DevOps engineer wants to ensure that the changes will not cause unintended resource replacements and that the new template adheres to organizational security policies. Which two AWS services or features should the engineer use? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["CloudFormation Change Sets","CloudFormation Guard","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Config","AWS Service Catalog"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (CloudFormation Change Sets) allow the engineer to preview the proposed changes to the stack resources, showing what will be added, modified, or deleted, thus preventing unintended replacements. Option B (CloudFormation Guard) enables policy-as-code compliance checking, allowing the engineer to validate the new template against organizational security policies before deployment. Option C (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) enforces configuration on running instances, not for pre-deployment validation. Option D (AWS Config) assesses deployed resources, not templates before deployment. Option E (AWS Service Catalog) is for standardized provisioning.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_75',
  'Which two AWS services or tools allow you to define your cloud infrastructure programmatically using general-purpose programming languages or declarative templates? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS CloudFormation","AWS CDK","AWS Systems Manager","AWS Config","AWS Service Catalog"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS CloudFormation) allows you to define your infrastructure using declarative JSON or YAML templates. Option B (AWS CDK) allows you to define your cloud infrastructure using familiar programming languages like Python, TypeScript, Java, C#, and Go. Option C (AWS Systems Manager) is for operational management and automation of running instances. Option D (AWS Config) assesses and monitors resource configurations. Option E (AWS Service Catalog) is for managing and provisioning approved IT services, often built on CloudFormation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_76',
  'A company wants to ensure that all EC2 instances launched within their AWS accounts consistently adhere to specific security configurations, such as firewall rules, software installations, and agent deployments. They need an automated solution to enforce this desired state and remediate any deviations. Which AWS Systems Manager capabilities are best suited for this task? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Systems Manager Patch Manager to ensure operating systems are up to date.","Systems Manager Inventory to collect software and configuration data from instances.","Systems Manager State Manager to define and apply desired state configurations.","Systems Manager Run Command to execute commands on instances on demand.","Systems Manager Session Manager to provide secure shell access to instances."]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option C (correct) is specifically designed to define and apply desired state configurations to instances, ensuring they consistently adhere to specified security configurations and automatically remediating any drift. Option A (correct) is crucial for maintaining the security posture of instances by ensuring their operating systems and applications are up to date with the latest security patches, which is a key aspect of security configuration. Option B (incorrect) collects data about instances but does not enforce or remediate configurations. Option D (incorrect) executes commands on demand but does not continuously enforce a desired state. Option E (incorrect) provides secure access but is not a configuration management tool.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_77',
  'A DevOps team needs to manage the configuration of a large fleet of EC2 instances, ensuring that they consistently run specific software versions and have required security agents installed. They want to automate the process of collecting configuration data and applying updates without manual intervention. Which AWS Systems Manager features are most relevant for these requirements? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Systems Manager State Manager for defining and enforcing desired configurations.","Systems Manager Parameter Store for securely storing configuration data.","Systems Manager Patch Manager for automating OS and application updates.","Systems Manager Automation for creating custom runbooks for operational tasks.","Systems Manager Session Manager for interactive access to instances."]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (correct) allows the team to define a desired state for their EC2 instances, ensuring consistent software versions and agent installations, and automatically remediating any configuration drift. Option C (correct) automates the process of scanning instances for missing patches and applying updates to operating systems and applications, which is critical for maintaining security and software versions across a large fleet. Option B (incorrect) is for storing sensitive data and configurations, but not for actively managing or enforcing instance configurations. Option D (incorrect) is for automating operational tasks through runbooks, but State Manager and Patch Manager are more direct for continuous configuration and patching. Option E (incorrect) provides secure interactive access, which is not directly related to automated configuration management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_78',
  'A DevOps team is managing a fleet of EC2 instances and needs to ensure they are consistently patched with the latest security updates. They also want to collect detailed information about the software installed on these instances for auditing and compliance purposes. Which AWS Systems Manager capabilities are most suitable for these tasks? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Systems Manager State Manager to define desired configuration states.","Systems Manager Patch Manager to automate the patching process for instances.","Systems Manager Inventory to gather software and configuration details from instances.","Systems Manager Automation to create custom operational runbooks.","Systems Manager Session Manager for secure remote access."]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (correct) is specifically designed to automate the process of scanning instances for missing patches and applying security updates, directly addressing the patching requirement. Option C (correct) is used to collect detailed information about the software, applications, and configurations on managed instances, which is essential for auditing and compliance purposes. Option A (incorrect) is for enforcing a desired configuration state, which is related but not the primary tool for patching or inventory collection. Option D (incorrect) is for automating general operational tasks, while Patch Manager and Inventory are more specialized for these specific needs. Option E (incorrect) provides secure interactive access to instances, which is unrelated to automated patching or inventory collection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_79',
  'A company is migrating legacy applications to AWS and needs to manage the configuration of their EC2 instances using a declarative approach. They want to ensure that specific software packages are installed and services are running consistently across their fleet. Which AWS services or features can be used to achieve this configuration management goal? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Systems Manager State Manager for defining and enforcing desired configurations.","AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate to manage configurations using Chef cookbooks.","AWS Service Catalog for provisioning pre-configured EC2 instances.","AWS CloudFormation to define the EC2 instance resources.","AWS Config to monitor configuration changes for compliance."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) allows defining a desired state for EC2 instances and continuously enforces that state, ensuring specific software is installed and services are running. Option B (correct) provides a managed service for Chef Automate, allowing users to manage instance configurations using Chef cookbooks, which is a declarative approach for configuration management, especially relevant for legacy migrations. Option C (incorrect) is for providing a catalog of approved products for self-service, not for ongoing configuration management. Option D (incorrect) defines the infrastructure (the EC2 instance itself) but doesn''t manage the *configuration* within the instance after it''s launched. Option E (incorrect) monitors configuration changes for compliance but does not actively manage or enforce the configuration itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_80',
  'A company needs to ensure that their AWS infrastructure configurations, including EC2 instance settings and security group rules, remain consistent over time and automatically revert any unauthorized changes. They also want to track the configuration history of their resources for auditing purposes. Which AWS services or features can fulfill these requirements? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Systems Manager State Manager for enforcing desired state configurations.","AWS Config for recording configuration changes and evaluating compliance.","AWS CloudFormation Change Sets for previewing infrastructure updates.","AWS Service Catalog for provisioning standardized resources.","AWS CloudFormation Guard for pre-deployment policy validation."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is designed to define and enforce a desired state configuration across EC2 instances, automatically remediating any drift from the specified configuration. Option B (correct) continuously records configuration changes of AWS resources, providing a detailed history and enabling evaluation against desired configurations or compliance rules, which is crucial for auditing and tracking consistency. Option C (incorrect) is for previewing *intended* changes from a CloudFormation template, not for enforcing runtime configuration or tracking changes. Option D (incorrect) is for providing a catalog of approved resources for self-service, not for enforcing configuration or tracking changes. Option E (incorrect) is for validating templates against policies *before* deployment, not for managing runtime configuration or tracking changes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

