VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_81',
  'A DevOps team is managing a large fleet of EC2 instances and needs to automate the process of collecting detailed software and application inventory data. They also want to ensure that these instances are always running the latest approved operating system patches. Which AWS Systems Manager capabilities are most appropriate for these operational tasks? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Systems Manager Inventory for collecting detailed information about managed instances.","Systems Manager Patch Manager for automating the application of OS and software updates.","Systems Manager State Manager for enforcing desired configuration states.","Systems Manager Run Command for executing arbitrary commands on instances.","Systems Manager Session Manager for secure interactive access to instances."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is specifically designed to collect detailed information about the software, applications, and configurations on managed instances, directly addressing the inventory data requirement. Option B (correct) automates the process of scanning instances for missing patches and applying security updates, ensuring instances are running the latest approved operating system patches. Option C (incorrect) is for enforcing a desired configuration state, which is related but not the primary tool for inventory collection or patching. Option D (incorrect) executes commands on demand but does not provide continuous inventory or patching automation. Option E (incorrect) provides secure interactive access to instances, which is unrelated to automated inventory or patching.',
  NOW(),
