  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_82',
  'A company wants to move away from manual configuration of their EC2 instances to an automated, desired-state configuration management approach. They need a service that can ensure instances are configured consistently and automatically remediate any deviations from the baseline. Which AWS services are suitable for this purpose? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Systems Manager State Manager for defining and enforcing desired state configurations.","AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate for managing configurations using Chef cookbooks.","AWS CloudFormation to define the EC2 instance resources.","AWS Config to monitor configuration changes for compliance.","AWS Service Catalog for provisioning pre-configured EC2 instances."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is a key component of AWS Systems Manager that allows defining a desired state for instances and continuously enforces that state, automatically remediating any configuration drift. Option B (correct) provides a managed service for Chef Automate, which uses Chef cookbooks to define and apply desired configurations to instances, offering a robust solution for automated configuration management. Option C (incorrect) defines the infrastructure itself (the EC2 instance), but not the ongoing configuration *within* the instance. Option D (incorrect) monitors configuration changes for compliance but does not actively manage or enforce the configuration. Option E (incorrect) is for providing a catalog of approved products for self-service, not for ongoing configuration management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_83',
  'A company wants to manage the configuration of its EC2 instances using a declarative model, ensuring that specific software is installed and services are running. They are considering using a legacy configuration management tool that relies on Chef cookbooks. Which AWS service is designed to support this approach? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate for a fully managed Chef server.","AWS Systems Manager State Manager for desired state configuration.","AWS CloudFormation to define the EC2 instance resources.","AWS Service Catalog to provision pre-configured instances.","AWS Config for auditing configuration changes."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) provides a fully managed Chef Automate server, allowing users to leverage existing Chef cookbooks and recipes for declarative configuration management of their EC2 instances. Option B (correct) also offers a declarative approach to configuration management, allowing users to define a desired state for their instances using Systems Manager Documents, which can include installing software and managing services. While OpsWorks is specifically for Chef, State Manager is a more general AWS-native declarative configuration management tool. Option C (incorrect) is for defining the infrastructure itself, not for ongoing configuration management within the instance. Option D (incorrect) is for providing a catalog of approved products for self-service, not for ongoing configuration management. Option E (incorrect) monitors configuration changes for compliance but does not actively manage or enforce the configuration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
