  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon Route 53 Geolocation routing) directs users to endpoints based on their geographic location, minimizing latency. Option B (AWS Global Accelerator) uses the AWS global network to route traffic to the optimal healthy endpoint, also reducing latency and improving availability. AWS Fault Injection Service (Option C) is for testing resilience. Amazon DynamoDB Global Tables (Option D) is a database service. AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (Option E) is for server replication.',
