  'Implementing a custom resource starts by creating an AWS Lambda function (Option A) that will contain the logic for handling the custom resource''s lifecycle events (Create, Update, Delete). You then grant the necessary permissions to this Lambda function (Option C) so it can interact with other AWS services. Next, you define the custom resource type within your CloudFormation template (Option B), referencing the Lambda function''s ARN. Finally, you deploy the CloudFormation stack (Option D), which triggers the Lambda function for the custom resource.',
