  '{0,2,3,1}',
  'To use conditions, first, Option A (Define the condition in the ''Conditions'' section) is where the condition block resides. Then, Option C (Specify a logical ID for the condition) gives it a unique identifier. Option D (Use intrinsic functions like ''Fn::Equals'' or ''Fn::And'' to define the condition logic) builds the actual conditional expression. Finally, Option B (Reference the condition in a resource or resource property) applies the condition using the `Condition` attribute.',
