VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_1_155',
  'A DevOps team is developing a new application using AWS CDK in Python. They need to create a new Amazon S3 bucket, an AWS Lambda function, and an Amazon DynamoDB table. Order the steps to define and deploy these resources using AWS CDK.',
  'ordering',
  '["Synthesize the CDK application into a CloudFormation template using `cdk synth`.","Write the CDK application code in Python, defining the S3 bucket, Lambda function, and DynamoDB table.","Deploy the synthesized CloudFormation stack to the AWS account using `cdk deploy`.","Initialize the CDK project in the target AWS account and Region using `cdk bootstrap` (if not already done)."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'Deploying an AWS CDK application involves a specific sequence of actions. Option B (Write the CDK application code in Python) is the initial step, where the infrastructure is defined programmatically. Next, Option A (Synthesize the CDK application into a CloudFormation template using `cdk synth`) translates the CDK code into a CloudFormation template. Option D (Initialize the CDK project in the target AWS account and Region using `cdk bootstrap`) must be performed to provision necessary resources for CDK deployments, if not already completed. Finally, Option C (Deploy the synthesized CloudFormation stack to the AWS account using `cdk deploy`) provisions the defined infrastructure in the AWS account.',
