  'Integrating CloudFormation Guard into a CI/CD pipeline starts with developing your AWS CloudFormation templates (Option C). Concurrently, you define your CloudFormation Guard policies (Option B) that specify your infrastructure compliance rules. Then, you add a pipeline stage to run CloudFormation Guard validation (Option A) against your templates and policies. Crucially, the pipeline should be configured to fail (Option D) if CloudFormation Guard detects any non-compliance, preventing non-compliant infrastructure from being deployed.',
