VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_99',
  'A DevOps team needs to ensure all EC2 instances are consistently configured with specific software. Order the steps to configure AWS Systems Manager State Manager to enforce a desired state.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an association in State Manager, targeting instances based on tags or IDs","Define a Systems Manager document specifying the desired configuration (e.g., installing software)","Specify the schedule and compliance reporting options for the association","Review the compliance status of instances in the Systems Manager console"]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To enforce a desired state, first, Option B (Define a Systems Manager document specifying the desired configuration) outlines the configuration steps. Then, Option A (Create an association in State Manager, targeting instances based on tags or IDs) links this document to the relevant instances. Option C (Specify the schedule and compliance reporting options for the association) dictates when and how often the configuration is applied and reported. Finally, Option D (Review the compliance status of instances in the Systems Manager console) allows monitoring of the configuration adherence.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_100',
  'A DevOps team needs to ensure that all Amazon EC2 instances across their development and production environments maintain a consistent software configuration and security patches. They have decided to use AWS Systems Manager State Manager and Patch Manager for this purpose. Order the steps to configure State Manager to enforce a desired configuration and Patch Manager for patching.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS Systems Manager Association in State Manager, linking the document to target EC2 instances.","Define a Systems Manager document (e.g., `AWS-RunShellScript`) that specifies the desired configuration state.","Configure AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager to define patch baselines and schedules.","Install the SSM Agent on all target EC2 instances and ensure it has the necessary IAM permissions."]'::json,
  '{3,1,0,2}',
  'To enforce desired configuration and patching with AWS Systems Manager, a specific setup sequence is required. Option D (Install the SSM Agent on all target EC2 instances and ensure it has the necessary IAM permissions) is the prerequisite, allowing Systems Manager to interact with the instances. Next, Option B (Define a Systems Manager document) specifies the configuration script or state to be enforced. Option A (Create an AWS Systems Manager Association in State Manager) then applies this document to the target instances, ensuring continuous enforcement. Finally, Option C (Configure AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager to define patch baselines and schedules) is set up separately to manage security updates, working in conjunction with State Manager for comprehensive instance management. This directly addresses anti-pattern ap-2.2-001 by automating configuration management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_101',
  'A company needs to automate the patching of their Amazon EC2 instances across various environments (development, staging, production) on a regular basis, ensuring minimal downtime and adherence to approved patch baselines. They choose AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager for this task. Order the steps to deploy and configure Patch Manager for an EC2 fleet.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a patch baseline that specifies approved and rejected patches for different operating systems.","Install the SSM Agent on all target EC2 instances and ensure it has the necessary IAM permissions.","Create a maintenance window to schedule when patching operations can occur.","Configure a Patch Manager patch group and associate it with the patch baseline and maintenance window."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Deploying AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager involves preparing instances, defining patch rules, and then scheduling the operations. Option B (Install the SSM Agent on all target EC2 instances and ensure it has the necessary IAM permissions) is the fundamental prerequisite for Systems Manager to manage instances. Next, Option A (Define a patch baseline) specifies which patches are approved or rejected. Option C (Create a maintenance window) defines the time slots during which patching can safely occur. Finally, Option D (Configure a Patch Manager patch group and associate it with the patch baseline and maintenance window) ties all these components together, initiating the automated patching process for the specified EC2 fleet.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  77,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_102',
  'A large-scale application processes orders through a complex workflow involving multiple microservices, data transformations, and human approvals. The DevOps team wants to orchestrate this workflow using AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda functions to ensure reliability and observability. Order the steps to build and deploy this complex automation.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the state machine using Amazon States Language, specifying the sequence of Lambda function invocations and decision points.","Deploy the Step Functions state machine and associated AWS Lambda functions.","Develop individual AWS Lambda functions for each step of the workflow (e.g., process order, validate inventory, send notification).","Create IAM roles with appropriate permissions for the Step Functions state machine and Lambda functions."]'::json,
  '{2,3,0,1}',
  'Building a complex automation workflow with AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda requires a structured approach. Option C (Develop individual AWS Lambda functions for each step of the workflow) is the initial step, creating the modular components of the workflow. Next, Option D (Create IAM roles with appropriate permissions for the Step Functions state machine and Lambda functions) establishes the necessary security context. Option A (Define the state machine using Amazon States Language) then orchestrates these Lambda functions into a coherent workflow. Finally, Option B (Deploy the Step Functions state machine and associated AWS Lambda functions) provisions the entire automated solution in AWS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  78,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_103',
  'A security team needs to create a custom AWS Config rule to evaluate whether specific Amazon EC2 instances have a particular tag value, which is not covered by existing managed rules. If an instance is non-compliant, they want to automatically remediate it. Order the steps to create and deploy this custom AWS Config rule with an automated remediation action.',
  'ordering',
  '["Deploy the AWS Config custom rule and the remediation action using CloudFormation.","Develop an AWS Lambda function that evaluates the compliance of EC2 instances based on the tag value.","Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document that adds the required tag to non-compliant EC2 instances.","Configure the AWS Config rule to trigger the Systems Manager Automation document as a remediation action."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'Creating a custom AWS Config rule with automated remediation involves defining the logic, the fix, and then linking them. Option B (Develop an AWS Lambda function that evaluates the compliance of EC2 instances based on the tag value) is the core logic for detecting non-compliance. Next, Option C (Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document that adds the required tag to non-compliant EC2 instances) defines the automated fix. Option D (Configure the AWS Config rule to trigger the Systems Manager Automation document as a remediation action) then connects the detection to the remediation. Finally, Option A (Deploy the AWS Config custom rule and the remediation action using CloudFormation) provisions these components in AWS, ensuring consistent and automated compliance enforcement.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  79,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_104',
  'A company has a hybrid cloud environment with on-premises servers that need to be managed and configured consistently with their Amazon EC2 instances. They want to extend AWS Systems Manager capabilities, such as State Manager and Inventory, to these on-premises servers. Order the steps to integrate on-premises servers with AWS Systems Manager.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an IAM service role for Systems Manager to interact with on-premises servers.","Install the SSM Agent on the on-premises servers and register them with Systems Manager.","Create an activation code in Systems Manager for registering on-premises servers.","Verify the on-premises servers appear in Systems Manager Fleet Manager and apply State Manager associations."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'Integrating on-premises servers with AWS Systems Manager requires a specific sequence of permission setup, registration, and verification. Option A (Create an IAM service role for Systems Manager to interact with on-premises servers) is the initial step, providing the necessary permissions for Systems Manager to manage hybrid environments. Next, Option C (Create an activation code in Systems Manager for registering on-premises servers) generates the credentials needed for the SSM Agent to connect. Option B (Install the SSM Agent on the on-premises servers and register them with Systems Manager) then performs the actual installation and registration. Finally, Option D (Verify the on-premises servers appear in Systems Manager Fleet Manager and apply State Manager associations) confirms successful integration and allows for management tasks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  80,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_105',
  'A DevOps team wants to build an automated pipeline to create and distribute securely patched Amazon Machine Images (AMIs) for their application, ensuring all instances are launched from up-to-date images. They plan to use AWS Systems Manager Automation documents and EC2 Image Builder. Order the steps to create this automated AMI patching pipeline.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define an EC2 Image Builder image pipeline that uses a Systems Manager Automation document as a build component.","Create a Systems Manager Automation document that applies security patches and performs custom hardening steps.","Configure the Image Builder pipeline to output a new AMI and distribute it to target accounts/Regions.","Specify a base AMI and instance type for the Image Builder pipeline."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'Building an automated AMI patching pipeline with Systems Manager Automation and EC2 Image Builder involves defining the patching logic, the base image, and the build process. Option B (Create a Systems Manager Automation document that applies security patches and performs custom hardening steps) is the core logic for updating the image. Next, Option D (Specify a base AMI and instance type for the Image Builder pipeline) defines the starting point for the image creation. Option A (Define an EC2 Image Builder image pipeline that uses a Systems Manager Automation document as a build component) then integrates the patching logic into the image creation workflow. Finally, Option C (Configure the Image Builder pipeline to output a new AMI and distribute it to target accounts/Regions) completes the pipeline by making the patched AMI available for use.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  81,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_106',
  'A company needs to collect inventory data (e.g., installed applications, network configurations, services) from all their Amazon EC2 instances and on-premises servers across multiple AWS Regions for auditing and compliance purposes. They decide to use AWS Systems Manager Inventory. Order the steps to set up Systems Manager Inventory for a hybrid fleet.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure an AWS Systems Manager Association to collect inventory data from target instances.","Ensure the SSM Agent is installed and running on all EC2 instances and on-premises servers.","Create an IAM instance profile or service role with permissions for SSM Agent to send inventory data.","View the collected inventory data in the Systems Manager console or query it using AWS CLI/SDK."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Setting up AWS Systems Manager Inventory for a hybrid fleet involves ensuring agent presence, granting permissions, configuring collection, and then reviewing data. Option B (Ensure the SSM Agent is installed and running on all EC2 instances and on-premises servers) is the fundamental prerequisite for data collection. Next, Option C (Create an IAM instance profile or service role with permissions for SSM Agent to send inventory data) grants the necessary permissions. Option A (Configure an AWS Systems Manager Association to collect inventory data from target instances) then defines what data to collect and how often. Finally, Option D (View the collected inventory data in the Systems Manager console or query it using AWS CLI/SDK) allows for analysis and auditing of the collected information.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  82,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_107',
  'A global enterprise needs to execute a standard set of operational tasks, such as restarting services or applying configuration updates, across Amazon EC2 instances in different AWS Regions and accounts. They want to centralize and automate these operations using AWS Systems Manager Automation documents. Order the steps to create and execute a cross-Region/cross-account Automation document.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Automation document that defines the operational task (e.g., `AWS-RestartEC2Instance`).","Configure cross-account/cross-Region permissions for Systems Manager in the target accounts and Regions.","Execute the Automation document, specifying target accounts, Regions, and instance filters.","Ensure the SSM Agent is installed and running on all target EC2 instances with appropriate IAM permissions."]'::json,
  '{3,1,0,2}',
  'Executing cross-Region/cross-account AWS Systems Manager Automation requires careful preparation of permissions and document definition. Option D (Ensure the SSM Agent is installed and running on all target EC2 instances with appropriate IAM permissions) is the fundamental prerequisite for Systems Manager to manage instances. Next, Option B (Configure cross-account/cross-Region permissions for Systems Manager in the target accounts and Regions) establishes the necessary trust relationships for the Automation to operate across boundaries. Option A (Create an Automation document that defines the operational task) then specifies the actual steps to be performed. Finally, Option C (Execute the Automation document, specifying target accounts, Regions, and instance filters) initiates the automated operation across the distributed fleet.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  83,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_108',
  'A company is migrating an application that relies on Chef cookbooks for configuration management. They decide to use AWS OpsWorks Stacks to manage their EC2 instances and automate the deployment of their application. Order the steps to set up and deploy an application using AWS OpsWorks Stacks.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an OpsWorks Stack, defining its Region, VPC, and default operating system.","Deploy the application to the instances within the OpsWorks Stack.","Create layers within the Stack (e.g., App Server, Database) and add EC2 instances to them.","Upload Chef cookbooks to an Amazon S3 bucket and configure the Stack to use them."]'::json,
  '{0,3,2,1}',
  'Setting up and deploying an application with AWS OpsWorks Stacks involves defining the environment, configuring Chef, and then deploying the application. Option A (Create an OpsWorks Stack, defining its Region, VPC, and default operating system) is the foundational step for the environment. Next, Option D (Upload Chef cookbooks to an Amazon S3 bucket and configure the Stack to use them) prepares the configuration management logic. Option C (Create layers within the Stack and add EC2 instances to them) then organizes the instances and applies the Chef recipes. Finally, Option B (Deploy the application to the instances within the OpsWorks Stack) initiates the application deployment, leveraging the configured Chef cookbooks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  84,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_37_m_37_3_109',
  'A DevOps team is managing a large fleet of Amazon EC2 instances and needs to ensure that specific security agents are always installed and running. They want to use AWS Systems Manager State Manager to continuously enforce this desired state. Order the steps to configure State Manager for continuous configuration compliance.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS Systems Manager Association to apply the document to the target EC2 instances.","Define a Systems Manager document (e.g., `AWS-RunShellScript`) that installs and verifies the security agent.","Install the SSM Agent on all target EC2 instances and ensure it has the necessary IAM permissions.","Monitor the compliance status of the instances in Systems Manager State Manager and remediate non-compliant instances."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'Configuring AWS Systems Manager State Manager for continuous configuration compliance involves preparing instances, defining the desired state, applying it, and then monitoring. Option C (Install the SSM Agent on all target EC2 instances and ensure it has the necessary IAM permissions) is the fundamental prerequisite for Systems Manager to manage instances. Next, Option B (Define a Systems Manager document) specifies the configuration script or state to be enforced. Option A (Create an AWS Systems Manager Association) then applies this document to the target instances, ensuring continuous enforcement. Finally, Option D (Monitor the compliance status of the instances in Systems Manager State Manager and remediate non-compliant instances) allows for ongoing oversight and corrective actions, directly addressing anti-pattern ap-2.2-001 by automating configuration management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain37_8',
  NOW(),
  85,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_37_3',
  'hard'
);

