  'A DevOps engineer is designing a chaos engineering experiment to test the resilience of an application''s database layer. Order the steps to set up a basic experiment using AWS Fault Injection Service (FIS).',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the actions to inject faults (e.g., terminate EC2 instances, throttle API calls).","Identify the target resources for the experiment (e.g., specific EC2 instances, RDS databases).","Create an FIS experiment template.","Start the FIS experiment and monitor its impact on the application."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Setting up a chaos engineering experiment with AWS FIS begins by identifying the target resources (Option B) that will be subjected to the fault injection. Next, the specific actions to inject faults are defined (Option A), such as terminating EC2 instances or throttling API calls. Once targets and actions are clear, an FIS experiment template is created (Option C) to encapsulate these definitions. Finally, the FIS experiment is started, and its impact on the application is monitored (Option D) to observe how the system behaves under stress, aligning with chaos engineering principles to proactively find weaknesses.',
