VALUES (
  'q_38_m_38_1_111',
  'Arrange the steps to deploy AWS Global Accelerator for an application.',
  'ordering',
  '["Add endpoints (e.g., Application Load Balancers, EC2 instances) to the endpoint group","Create a Global Accelerator accelerator","Configure listeners and endpoint groups for the accelerator","Route client traffic to the accelerator''s static IP addresses or DNS name"]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Deploying AWS Global Accelerator starts with creating a Global Accelerator accelerator (Option B), which provides static IP addresses. Next, you configure listeners and endpoint groups (Option C) to define how traffic is received and where it should be routed. Then, you add your application endpoints (Option A) to the appropriate endpoint groups. Finally, you route client traffic to the accelerator''s static IP addresses or DNS name (Option D) to leverage its global network for performance and availability.',
