  'Option C (correct) refers to the Amazon CloudWatch Agent, which is specifically designed to collect logs and system-level metrics from Amazon EC2 instances, on-premises servers, and virtual machines, and send them to Amazon CloudWatch. Option A is for distributed tracing. Option B is for event-driven automation. Option D records AWS API calls and related events, not application logs or system metrics from instances directly.',
