VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_3_91',
  'To ensure artifact immutability in a CI/CD pipeline, specific practices are followed. Order these actions to implement an immutable container image strategy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Tag the image with a unique, non-reusable identifier (e.g., Git SHA)","Build the container image","Push the tagged image to Amazon ECR","Reference the immutable tag in deployments"]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Implementing an immutable container image strategy begins with Option B (Build the container image). After building, Option A (Tag the image with a unique, non-reusable identifier) ensures that each image version is uniquely identifiable and prevents accidental overwrites. Then, Option C (Push the tagged image to Amazon ECR) stores the immutable artifact. Finally, Option D (Reference the immutable tag in deployments) ensures that deployments always use a specific, known version of the image, which is critical for reproducibility and rollback.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_3_92',
  'A developer wants to consume packages from an existing AWS CodeArtifact npm repository. Order the steps to configure their local npm client.',
  'ordering',
  '["Install packages using `npm install`","Get the authorization token from CodeArtifact","Configure npm registry to point to CodeArtifact","Login to CodeArtifact using the token"]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}',
  'To consume packages from a CodeArtifact npm repository, the first step is Option C (Configure npm registry to point to CodeArtifact) to tell npm where to find the repository. Next, Option B (Get the authorization token from CodeArtifact) retrieves the temporary credentials. Then, Option D (Login to CodeArtifact using the token) authenticates the npm client. Finally, Option A (Install packages using `npm install`) can be used to download and install dependencies from the repository.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_3',
  'easy'
);

