  '["Configure npm to use the CodeArtifact repository endpoint and authentication token.","Create an AWS CodeArtifact domain.","Generate an authentication token for CodeArtifact using the AWS CLI.","Create a repository within the CodeArtifact domain."]'::json,
  '{1,3,2,0}',
  'To set up CodeArtifact, you first create a domain, which acts as a container for repositories (Option B). Next, you create a repository within that domain to store your packages (Option D). After the repository is ready, you generate an authentication token using the AWS CLI, which npm will use to interact with CodeArtifact (Option C). Finally, you configure npm to use the CodeArtifact repository endpoint and the generated token for publishing and consuming packages (Option A).',
