  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'Implementing an immutable artifact strategy starts by building the Docker image (Option B) from the source code. Next, the image must be tagged with a unique identifier (Option D), such as a Git commit SHA, to ensure immutability and traceability (anti-pattern: using mutable tags like ''latest''). This uniquely tagged image is then pushed to Amazon ECR (Option A). Finally, the deployment manifest (Option C) is updated to reference this specific, immutable image tag, ensuring that the deployed version is always precisely identifiable.',
