  'To set up S3 cross-region replication, you must first enable versioning on both the source and destination S3 buckets (Option B), as it''s a prerequisite for replication. Next, create an IAM role (Option A) that grants Amazon S3 the necessary permissions to replicate objects. Then, define a replication rule (Option C) on the source bucket, specifying the destination bucket and the IAM role created. Finally, verify the setup (Option D) by uploading a new object to ensure it replicates successfully.',
