  'The correct order for publishing a package to AWS CodeArtifact begins with setting up the infrastructure. Option B (Create a CodeArtifact domain and a repository within that domain) establishes the necessary CodeArtifact resources. Next, Option C (Authenticate your local environment to CodeArtifact to obtain a temporary authorization token) is crucial for granting permissions to interact with the repository. Following authentication, Option A (Configure your local build tool to use the CodeArtifact repository endpoint) directs your tool to the correct location. Finally, Option D (Publish the package to the CodeArtifact repository using your build tool) executes the upload of your package.',
