  'The logical sequence for setting up AWS CodeArtifact begins with the highest-level resource. Option B (Create a new CodeArtifact domain) is the first step, as a domain is a logical grouping for repositories. Next, Option C (Create a new CodeArtifact repository within the domain) establishes the actual storage for packages. After the domain is created, Option D (Set resource policies for the domain to control access) defines who can access the domain and its repositories. Finally, Option A (Configure the repository''s upstream sources, if any, to pull packages from public repositories or other CodeArtifact repositories) is an optional but common step to integrate with other package sources.',
