  'ordering',
  '["Update the CI/CD pipeline to use the immutable image tag for deployments.","Configure the build process to tag container images with a unique identifier, such as a Git commit SHA or a build number.","Push the uniquely tagged container image to Amazon ECR.","Remove any usage of mutable tags like ''latest'' from the deployment process."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Implementing an immutable artifact strategy starts with ensuring unique identification. Option B (Configure the build process to tag container images with a unique identifier) is the first step to create an immutable tag. Then, Option C (Push the uniquely tagged container image to Amazon ECR) stores this immutable artifact. Once the image is available, Option A (Update the CI/CD pipeline to use the immutable image tag for deployments) ensures that deployments reference this specific, unchanging version. Finally, Option D (Remove any usage of mutable tags like ''latest'' from the deployment process) is crucial to prevent the anti-pattern of mutable tags (ap-1.3-001) and ensure reproducibility.',
