INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_81',
  'A team is deploying a new version of an AWS Lambda function and wants to use AWS CodeDeploy for controlled deployments. Order the steps to set up a CodeDeploy application and deployment group for a Lambda function.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS CodeDeploy application of compute platform ''AWS Lambda''.","Define the `AppSpec` file to specify the Lambda function details and traffic shifting configuration.","Create a deployment group within the application, specifying the Lambda function name and an optional pre-traffic hook.","Grant the CodeDeploy service role permissions to invoke Lambda functions and update aliases."]'::json,
  '{0,3,2,1}',
  'To set up CodeDeploy for Lambda, you first create an AWS CodeDeploy application, ensuring the compute platform is set to ''AWS Lambda'' (Option A). Next, the CodeDeploy service role needs permissions to invoke Lambda functions and manage aliases (Option D). Then, you create a deployment group within this application, specifying the target Lambda function and any pre-traffic hooks (Option C). Finally, you define the `AppSpec` file, which details the Lambda function version, its alias, and how traffic shifting should occur (Option B).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_82',
  'A developer is preparing to deploy an AWS Lambda function using AWS CodeDeploy and needs to define the deployment specifications. Order the steps to structure an `AppSpec` file for a CodeDeploy Lambda deployment.',
  'ordering',
  '["Specify the `version` and `Resources` section, defining the Lambda function to be deployed.","Create an `AppSpec` file (appspec.yml) in the root of your source bundle.","Define the `Hooks` section to specify Lambda functions to run before or after traffic shifting.","Include the `TargetService` section to specify the Lambda function''s alias and optional post-traffic test Lambda."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'To structure an `AppSpec` file for a Lambda deployment, you first create the `appspec.yml` file in the root of your source bundle (Option B). Then, you specify the `version` and the `Resources` section, which defines the specific Lambda function that CodeDeploy will manage (Option A). Next, you include the `TargetService` section, which specifies the Lambda function''s alias for traffic routing and can include a post-traffic test Lambda (Option D). Finally, you define the `Hooks` section, which allows you to specify Lambda functions to run as lifecycle hooks, such as `BeforeAllowTraffic` or `AfterAllowTraffic` (Option C).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_83',
  'A DevOps team wants to implement blue/green deployments for their Amazon ECS service using AWS CodeDeploy. Order the steps to configure CodeDeploy for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS CodeDeploy application with compute platform ''Amazon ECS''.","Define an `AppSpec` file that specifies the new Amazon ECS task definition and container details.","Create a deployment group, linking it to the ECS service, load balancer, and target groups for blue/green.","Ensure the CodeDeploy service role has permissions to manage ECS services, load balancers, and target groups."]'::json,
  '{0,3,2,1}',
  'To configure CodeDeploy for Amazon ECS blue/green deployments, you first create an AWS CodeDeploy application, setting the compute platform to ''Amazon ECS'' (Option A). Next, ensure the CodeDeploy service role has the necessary IAM permissions to interact with ECS, load balancers, and target groups (Option D). Then, create a deployment group, linking it to your Amazon ECS service, and specifying the Application Load Balancer and its blue and green target groups (Option C). Finally, define an `AppSpec` file that outlines the new ECS task definition, container details, and how traffic should be shifted (Option B).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_84',
  'A developer needs to add custom logic to run during an AWS CodeDeploy Lambda deployment, such as validation checks. Order the steps to set up CodeDeploy lifecycle hooks for a Lambda function.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create separate Lambda functions to act as lifecycle hooks (e.g., `BeforeAllowTraffic`, `AfterAllowTraffic`).","Define the `Hooks` section in the `AppSpec` file, referencing the ARN of the lifecycle hook Lambda functions.","Ensure the CodeDeploy service role has permissions to invoke these lifecycle hook Lambda functions.","Configure the CodeDeploy deployment group for the target Lambda function."]'::json,
  '{0,3,2,1}',
  'To set up CodeDeploy lifecycle hooks for a Lambda function, you first create the individual Lambda functions that will perform the custom logic at specific deployment stages (Option A). Next, you configure the CodeDeploy deployment group for your target Lambda function (Option D). The CodeDeploy service role must then be granted permissions to invoke these newly created lifecycle hook Lambda functions (Option C). Finally, you define the `Hooks` section in your `AppSpec` file, referencing the ARN of these lifecycle hook Lambda functions to execute them at the appropriate stages (Option B).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_85',
  'To enable AWS CodeDeploy to manage blue/green deployments for an Amazon ECS service, the ECS task definition needs specific configuration. Order the steps to prepare an Amazon ECS task definition for use with CodeDeploy for blue/green deployments.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a container within the task definition, specifying its image, ports, and other parameters.","Create a new Amazon ECS task definition.","Ensure the task definition references an image that is managed by Amazon ECR.","Specify the `containerName` and `containerPort` in the `AppSpec` file''s `TargetService` section that matches the task definition."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To prepare an ECS task definition for CodeDeploy blue/green, you first create a new Amazon ECS task definition (Option B). Within this task definition, you define the containers that will run, specifying their images, port mappings, and other configurations (Option A). It''s crucial that the task definition references a container image that is stored in and managed by Amazon ECR (Option C). Finally, when you create the CodeDeploy `AppSpec` file, you must ensure the `containerName` and `containerPort` in its `TargetService` section precisely match those defined in your ECS task definition (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_86',
  'A team is adopting a serverless architecture and needs to manage deployments of AWS Lambda functions. Order the steps to create a CodeDeploy application specifically for serverless deployments.',
  'ordering',
  '["Navigate to the AWS CodeDeploy service in the AWS Management Console.","Specify the application name and select ''AWS Lambda'' as the compute platform.","Click ''Create application''.","Review the details and confirm application creation."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To create a CodeDeploy application for serverless deployments, you first navigate to the AWS CodeDeploy service in the AWS Management Console (Option A). Then, you click the ''Create application'' button (Option C). Next, you specify a name for your application and, crucially, select ''AWS Lambda'' as the compute platform (Option B). Finally, you review the configuration details and confirm the creation of the application (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_87',
  'A CI/CD pipeline has built a new version of an AWS Lambda function and needs to deploy it using AWS CodeDeploy. Order the steps in a CodeDeploy deployment for a new Lambda function version.',
  'ordering',
  '["CodeDeploy shifts traffic from the old Lambda function version to the new version based on the deployment preference.","CodeDeploy creates a new version of the Lambda function and updates the alias to point to it.","CodeDeploy invokes optional pre-traffic hook Lambda functions.","CodeDeploy invokes optional post-traffic hook Lambda functions after traffic shifting is complete."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'During a CodeDeploy deployment for a Lambda function, the first step is that CodeDeploy creates the new version of the Lambda function and updates its alias to point to this new version (Option B). Then, CodeDeploy invokes any configured pre-traffic hook Lambda functions for validation (Option C). After successful pre-traffic hooks, CodeDeploy begins shifting traffic from the old Lambda version to the new one according to the specified deployment preference (Option A). Finally, after traffic shifting is complete, CodeDeploy invokes any configured post-traffic hook Lambda functions for final validation (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_88',
  'An Amazon ECS blue/green deployment managed by CodeDeploy has failed during the validation phase. Order the steps CodeDeploy would typically take for an automated rollback.',
  'ordering',
  '["CodeDeploy detects the failure based on configured CloudWatch alarms or deployment lifecycle hooks.","CodeDeploy automatically terminates the newly deployed (green) task set.","CodeDeploy reverts traffic routing to the original (blue) task set.","The ECS service continues to run the stable, original application version."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'In an automated rollback scenario for an ECS blue/green deployment, CodeDeploy first detects the failure (Option A) through configured CloudWatch alarms or failed lifecycle hooks. Upon detection, CodeDeploy immediately reverts traffic routing (Option C) back to the original, stable (blue) task set. Then, CodeDeploy automatically terminates the newly deployed (green) task set (Option B) that caused the failure. Finally, the ECS service continues to run the stable, original application version (Option D), ensuring service continuity (anti-pattern: not implementing automated rollback triggers).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_89',
  'A developer needs to update an existing AWS Lambda function with new code using an AWS CodePipeline. Order the steps for a successful deployment.',
  'ordering',
  '["CodePipeline detects the change in the source repository and starts execution.","AWS CodeBuild packages the updated Lambda function code and dependencies.","AWS CodeDeploy deploys the new version of the Lambda function.","The developer updates the Lambda function code in the source code repository (e.g., AWS CodeCommit)."]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}',
  'To update a Lambda function via CodePipeline, the process starts when the developer updates the Lambda function code (Option D) in the source repository. CodePipeline then detects this change (Option A) and initiates the pipeline execution. Next, AWS CodeBuild (Option B) packages the updated Lambda function code and its dependencies. Finally, AWS CodeDeploy (Option C) takes this package and deploys the new version of the Lambda function.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  67,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_90',
  'A company needs to deploy a new version of an EC2 instance-based application with minimal downtime using a blue/green deployment strategy. Order the steps for a successful deployment.',
  'ordering',
  '["Launch a new set of EC2 instances (the green environment) with the new application version.","Configure CodeDeploy to shift traffic from the original (blue) environment to the new (green) environment.","Perform thorough testing and validation on the green environment.","Terminate the old EC2 instances (the blue environment) after successful traffic shift and stabilization."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'For an EC2 blue/green deployment, you first launch a new set of EC2 instances (Option A) with the new application version, forming the ''green'' environment. Next, perform thorough testing and validation (Option C) on this green environment to ensure stability. Then, configure CodeDeploy (Option B) to shift traffic from the original ''blue'' environment to the new ''green'' environment. Finally, terminate the old EC2 instances (Option D) after the traffic shift is complete and the new environment is stable.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain36_8',
  NOW(),
  68,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_36_4',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_36_m_36_4_91',
  'An Amazon ECS service needs to be updated with a new task definition, and the team wants to use the default rolling update deployment type. Order the steps to perform this update.',
  'ordering',
  '["Update the Amazon ECS service, referencing the new task definition.","Define the ECS service with desired count and minimum healthy percent settings.","Register a new Amazon ECS task definition with the updated container image.","Amazon ECS replaces old tasks with new tasks based on the rolling update configuration."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'To update an ECS service with a rolling update, first register a new Amazon ECS task definition (Option C) containing the updated container image. Next, define the ECS service (Option B) with appropriate desired count and minimum healthy percent settings, which govern the rolling update behavior. Then, update the Amazon ECS service (Option A) to use the new task definition. Finally, Amazon ECS automatically replaces old tasks with new tasks (Option D) according to the rolling update configuration.',
