  'To deploy a containerized application to Amazon ECS using CodeDeploy Blue/Green, you first need the new application version. Option C (Define a task definition and a new image for the updated application version) prepares the container artifact. Next, Option B (Update the Amazon ECS service to use the CodeDeploy deployment controller) integrates CodeDeploy with the ECS service. Following this, Option A (Create an AWS CodeDeploy application and a deployment group) defines the deployment target and strategy. Finally, Option D (Initiate a deployment through CodeDeploy) triggers the Blue/Green deployment, including traffic shifting.',
