  '{2,0,3,1}',
  'The `AppSpec` file for AWS CodeDeploy has a specific structure. Option C (The `version` and `os` sections at the top of the file) are the mandatory initial declarations. Next, Option A (The `files` section to specify which files to copy and where) defines the source and destination for application files. Following this, Option D (The `permissions` section to set file and directory permissions) ensures proper access control. Finally, Option B (The `hooks` section to define scripts to run at various stages of the deployment lifecycle) specifies custom scripts to execute during deployment events.',
