  '{0,1,3,2}',
  'The typical execution sequence of AWS CodeDeploy lifecycle hooks for an in-place deployment is logical. Option A (ApplicationStop) is usually the first hook to gracefully stop the currently running application. Next, Option B (BeforeInstall) allows for preparatory tasks before the new application is installed. Following this, Option D (Install) handles the actual placement of new application files. Finally, Option C (ApplicationStart) starts the newly installed application.',
