  'To add a test stage, you first configure an AWS CodeBuild project specifically for running unit tests, ensuring it can consume the artifacts from the previous build stage (Option B). Next, you add a new stage to your CodePipeline, typically placed after the main build stage (Option A). Then, you specify this CodeBuild project as the action provider for the newly created test stage (Option C). Finally, you update the `buildspec.yml` file within the CodeBuild project to include the necessary commands to execute tests and generate test reports (Option D).',
