  'To implement a staging environment, you first add a new stage to your CodePipeline, placing it strategically after integration tests but before the production deployment stage (Option B). Next, configure this new staging stage to deploy the application to a dedicated, production-like staging environment (Option A). Within this staging stage, implement comprehensive automated tests, such as end-to-end and load tests, to validate the application thoroughly (Option C). Finally, to ensure quality gates, add a manual approval action after the staging deployment and tests, requiring explicit sign-off before the application proceeds to production (Option D). This addresses the anti-pattern of deploying to production without a staging environment.',
