INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_1_39',
  'What is the primary purpose of AWS Health events integration with Amazon EventBridge?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide detailed billing information for AWS services.","To enable automated responses to changes in AWS service health and resource state.","To store application logs for debugging purposes.","To manage user authentication and authorization."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (To enable automated responses to changes in AWS service health and resource state) is the correct answer. AWS Health integrates with Amazon EventBridge to allow customers to receive notifications and trigger automated actions based on events that affect their AWS resources, such as scheduled maintenance or service issues. Option A (To provide detailed billing information for AWS services) is handled by AWS Cost Explorer and AWS Billing. Option C (To store application logs for debugging purposes) is typically done with Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Option D (To manage user authentication and authorization) is handled by AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_40_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_1_40',
  'Which AWS service is best suited for distributing a single message to multiple subscribers using a fan-out pattern for various endpoints like email, SMS, or AWS Lambda functions?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon Kinesis","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon SNS) is the correct choice for a fan-out pattern to distribute a single message to multiple subscribers across different endpoint types. Option A (Amazon SQS) is a message queuing service used for decoupling and scaling microservices, typically for one-to-one or one-to-many processing where each message is consumed by a single consumer. Option C (Amazon Kinesis) is for real-time data streaming. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is a serverless workflow service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_40_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_1_41',
  'A security team needs to automatically remediate Amazon GuardDuty findings, such as compromised EC2 instances. Which AWS service can be triggered by a GuardDuty event via Amazon EventBridge to execute custom remediation logic?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","AWS Lambda","AWS CloudFormation","Amazon RDS"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Lambda) is the correct service. Amazon GuardDuty findings can be sent to Amazon EventBridge, which can then trigger an AWS Lambda function to execute custom code for automated remediation, such as isolating an EC2 instance or revoking temporary credentials. Option A (Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling) manages the scaling of EC2 instances. Option C (AWS CloudFormation) is for infrastructure as code. Option D (Amazon RDS) is a relational database service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_40_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_1_42',
  'What is the primary benefit of using Amazon SQS in an event-driven architecture for event distribution?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide real-time analytics on event streams.","To ensure messages are processed in strict FIFO order across multiple consumers.","To decouple components and buffer messages, allowing asynchronous processing and resilience.","To send push notifications directly to mobile devices."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (To decouple components and buffer messages, allowing asynchronous processing and resilience) is the primary benefit of Amazon SQS in event distribution. It acts as a buffer, ensuring that producers can send messages even if consumers are temporarily unavailable or overwhelmed. Option A (To provide real-time analytics on event streams) is a use case for services like Amazon Kinesis. Option B (To ensure messages are processed in strict FIFO order across multiple consumers) is a feature of Amazon SQS FIFO queues, but the general primary benefit is decoupling and buffering. Option D (To send push notifications directly to mobile devices) is a feature of Amazon SNS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_40_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_1_43',
  'Which AWS service allows you to create custom event patterns to filter and route events from various sources, including other AWS services and custom applications, to specific targets in a serverless manner?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Step Functions","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Glue","Amazon DynamoDB"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon EventBridge) is the correct service. It allows you to create rules with custom event patterns to filter and route events from many sources to various targets without provisioning or managing servers. Option A (AWS Step Functions) is for orchestrating workflows. Option C (AWS Glue) is an ETL service. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_40_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_1_44',
  'A developer wants to process events from a custom application and distribute them to multiple AWS Lambda functions for different processing tasks. Which AWS service is ideal for routing these custom events?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon EventBridge","AWS CloudFormation"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon EventBridge) is ideal for routing custom application events to multiple AWS Lambda functions. It allows defining rules based on event content to direct events to specific targets. Option A (Amazon SQS) is a queuing service, typically for one-to-one or one-to-many processing where each message is consumed once. Option B (Amazon SNS) is a publish/subscribe service, suitable for fan-out, but EventBridge offers more advanced content-based filtering and routing for custom events. Option D (AWS CloudFormation) is for infrastructure as code.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_40_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_1_45',
  'A DevOps team wants to receive notifications for AWS Health events that impact their resources and trigger an AWS Lambda function for automated remediation. Which service should be used to capture and route these AWS Health events?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudTrail","Amazon SQS","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon SNS"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon EventBridge) is the correct service. AWS Health events can be configured to send notifications to Amazon EventBridge, which can then filter these events and route them to targets like AWS Lambda functions for automated responses. Option A (AWS CloudTrail) records API calls and events but doesn''t directly route AWS Health events for automated processing. Option B (Amazon SQS) is a message queue. Option D (Amazon SNS) is a notification service, but EventBridge provides the direct integration and routing capabilities for AWS Health events.',
