  '{2}',
  'Option C (To automatically correct non-compliant resource configurations without human intervention) is the primary benefit. This feature allows AWS Config to detect non-compliant resources and automatically trigger predefined AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks to bring them back into compliance, significantly reducing operational overhead and improving security posture. Option A (To manually approve every configuration change) is the opposite of automation. Option B (To ensure all resources are always provisioned using CloudFormation) is a benefit of infrastructure as code, not specific to Config auto-remediation. Option D (To generate compliance reports for auditing) is a capability of AWS Config, but auto-remediation goes beyond reporting to active fixing.',
