  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter, which provides a central place for operations engineers to view, investigate, and resolve operational work items (OpsItems) that originate from various AWS services. It aggregates and standardizes operational issues, enabling faster resolution. Option B, AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager, is for structured incident response and escalation, not general operational issue tracking. Option C, Amazon EventBridge, is an event bus service for routing events, not for tracking operational issues. Option D, AWS Lambda, is a serverless compute service that can be part of a remediation workflow but does not provide a centralized dashboard for operational issues.',
