  'Option B (correct) is an AWS Config rule with an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook. AWS Config can continuously evaluate security group configurations against a rule. If non-compliance (e.g., unrestricted SSH access) is detected, it can automatically trigger a Systems Manager Automation runbook to modify the security group and remove the offending rule, providing a robust and automated solution. Option A requires custom Lambda code and logic for detection and remediation. Option C provides notification but not automated remediation. Option D represents an anti-pattern (ap-5.2-001) as manual remediation is not scalable.',
