VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_2_49',
  'A DevOps team needs to ensure that all Amazon EC2 instances and container images in their AWS accounts are continuously scanned for software vulnerabilities and unintended network exposure. Which AWS service should they use to achieve this with minimal operational overhead?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Security Hub","Amazon GuardDuty","Amazon Inspector v2","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Inspector v2) is the correct choice. Amazon Inspector v2 provides automated, continuous vulnerability management for Amazon EC2 instances and container images stored in Amazon ECR. It simplifies the process of identifying and reporting software vulnerabilities and network exposure. Option A (AWS Security Hub) aggregates findings but doesn''t perform the direct scanning. Option B (Amazon GuardDuty) focuses on threat detection, not vulnerability scanning of software. Option D (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations and compliance, not software vulnerabilities.',
