  'Option C (Service Control Policies (SCPs)) in AWS Organizations can be used to enforce preventive controls across all accounts, such as preventing new IAM users from creating S3 buckets. This is a broad, organizational-level control. Option A (IAM permission boundaries) apply to individual IAM entities. Option B (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) identifies external access. Option D (AWS Config rules) audit configurations.',
