  'Option A (AWS Config) is used to evaluate configurations and detect non-compliance. When a rule becomes non-compliant, AWS Config can send an event to Amazon EventBridge. Option B (AWS Lambda) can be configured as a target for an EventBridge rule, allowing it to execute the custom Python script in response to the Config non-compliance event. This provides a serverless way to automate custom remediation. Option C (Amazon SQS) is a message queue and would require another service to poll and trigger the script. Option D (AWS CloudFormation) is for infrastructure provisioning. Option E (Amazon SNS) is for sending notifications, not for executing custom scripts directly.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
