  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (AWS Config) is used to define desired configurations and detect non-compliance. Option C (AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks) can be integrated with AWS Config to automatically remediate non-compliant resources, providing a low-overhead solution for enforcing desired states. Option B (Manual remediation scripts) is incorrect because it requires significant operational overhead and does not scale. Option D (AWS Lambda functions without Config integration) could perform remediation but would require custom logic for detecting non-compliance and triggering, increasing operational overhead compared to Config''s native auto-remediation. Option E (AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter) is primarily for tracking operational issues and incidents, not for automated remediation execution itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
