  '{1,4}',
  'Option B (AWS Config) continuously monitors and records your AWS resource configurations and evaluates them against desired configurations. When a resource is non-compliant, AWS Config can trigger remediation actions. Option E (AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks) provides the actual automation documents that AWS Config can invoke to perform the remediation steps, such as modifying resource properties to bring them back into compliance. Option A (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus that can trigger actions but doesn''t define or assess compliance itself. Option C (AWS Lambda) can be a target for remediation but requires custom code and isn''t the primary service for defining and triggering compliance remediation. Option D (Amazon GuardDuty) is a threat detection service, not for configuration compliance.',
