  'Option B (Amazon EventBridge) can capture Amazon GuardDuty findings as events. Rules can then be set up to filter for critical threats and trigger automated actions. Option D (AWS Lambda) can be invoked by EventBridge to execute custom code, such as modifying security groups to quarantine the EC2 instance and logging the incident details. Option A (AWS Config) is for configuration compliance, not real-time threat response. Option C (AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter) is for tracking operational issues, not for executing the quarantine action itself. Option E (Amazon SNS) can send notifications but cannot perform the automated quarantine action.',
