  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon EventBridge) is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together using data from your own applications, integrated SaaS applications, and AWS services. It supports content-based filtering and routing to multiple targets. Option B (Amazon SNS) can also be used for fan-out patterns, distributing messages to multiple subscribers, including AWS Lambda, Amazon SQS, and HTTP/S endpoints, effectively routing events. Option C (AWS Lambda) is a compute service that executes code in response to events, but it doesn''t inherently provide event routing or filtering capabilities without custom code. Option D (AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter) is for operational issue tracking, not event routing. Option E (Amazon SQS) is a message queuing service, primarily for decoupling and buffering, not for complex event routing and filtering.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_40_1',
  'medium'
);

