  'Option A (Amazon SNS) is a messaging service that enables you to send messages to a large number of subscribers (fan-out pattern) asynchronously. Option D (Amazon EventBridge) can route events from a single source to multiple targets (consumers) based on rules, effectively performing a fan-out. Option B (Amazon SQS) is a queuing service primarily for one-to-one or one-to-many with polling, but not a direct fan-out from a single publisher to multiple distinct queues without an intermediary. Option C (AWS Lambda) is a compute service, not an event distribution service itself, though it can be a target. Option E (AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter) is for operational issue tracking, not event distribution.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain40_8',
  NOW(),
  36,
