  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (Amazon EventBridge) supports cross-account event routing, allowing events from a source account to be sent to an event bus in a different destination account. This centralizes event management. Option D (AWS Lambda) is a common target for EventBridge rules, including those receiving cross-account events, allowing for custom processing or remediation actions. Option A (Amazon SNS) and Option C (Amazon SQS) are messaging services that can receive events but are not primarily designed for cross-account event routing as an event bus. Option E (AWS Health) provides information about AWS service events.',
