  '["Amazon GuardDuty","Amazon SNS","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config","AWS WAF"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon GuardDuty) is a threat detection service that continuously monitors for malicious activity and unauthorized behavior, including suspicious API calls indicating unauthorized access. When GuardDuty detects such activity, it generates a finding. Option B (Amazon SNS) can be set up as a target for EventBridge rules that filter GuardDuty findings, allowing the security team to receive immediate notifications via email, SMS, or other protocols. Option C (AWS CloudTrail) records API activity but doesn''t actively detect threats or send alerts without integration. Option D (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations. Option E (AWS WAF) is a web application firewall.',
