  '["Configure network access (VPC or public) and fine-grained access control.","Specify the domain name and select the OpenSearch version.","Choose instance types, number of instances, and storage for data and master nodes.","Review the configuration and create the OpenSearch Service domain."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To create an Amazon OpenSearch Service domain, Option B (Specify the domain name and select the OpenSearch version) is the initial and fundamental step. Next, Option C (Choose instance types, number of instances, and storage for data and master nodes) defines the core infrastructure. After that, Option A (Configure network access (VPC or public) and fine-grained access control) secures and defines how the domain can be accessed. Finally, Option D (Review the configuration and create the OpenSearch Service domain) confirms and provisions the domain. Attempting to configure network access or review before defining the domain name and core infrastructure would be out of sequence.',
