VALUES (
  'q_39_m_39_1_123',
  'A company needs to centralize logs from various sources into Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, transform them with AWS Lambda, and then deliver them to Amazon S3. Order the following steps to set up this centralized logging architecture.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to use the Lambda function for data transformation.","Create an AWS Lambda function to process and transform incoming log records.","Create an Amazon S3 bucket for storing the transformed logs.","Configure Kinesis Data Firehose to deliver the transformed data to the S3 bucket."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'To set up centralized logging with Kinesis Data Firehose and Lambda transformation, Option C (Create an Amazon S3 bucket for storing the transformed logs) is the ultimate destination and should be created first. Next, Option B (Create an AWS Lambda function to process and transform incoming log records) defines the transformation logic. After that, Option A (Configure the Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to use the Lambda function for data transformation) integrates the Lambda function into the Firehose pipeline. Finally, Option D (Configure Kinesis Data Firehose to deliver the transformed data to the S3 bucket) directs the processed data to its final storage. Configuring Firehose before the S3 bucket or Lambda function exist would lead to an incomplete or invalid setup.',
