  'Option A (Amazon Macie) is a data security and data privacy service that uses machine learning and pattern matching to discover and protect sensitive data in AWS. It automatically detects sensitive data, including PII, in Amazon S3. Option B (AWS Security Hub) is essential for centralizing Macie''s findings, providing a consolidated view of security alerts and compliance status across accounts. Option C (AWS KMS) is used for managing encryption keys, which is crucial for protecting sensitive data but doesn''t identify the data itself. Option D (Amazon GuardDuty) is a threat detection service that monitors for malicious activity and unauthorized behavior, not data classification. Option E (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) helps identify resources shared with an external entity, focusing on access policies rather than data content.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
