  'Option A (VPC Flow Logs) capture information about the IP traffic going to and from network interfaces in your VPC, providing crucial data for network security analysis and troubleshooting. Option B (Amazon GuardDuty) can analyze VPC Flow Logs, along with CloudTrail events and DNS logs, to detect potential threats and malicious activity based on network patterns. Option C (AWS CloudTrail) logs API activity, not network traffic. Option D (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations, not network traffic. Option E (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) identifies external access to resources, not network traffic patterns or threats within the network.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_79',
  'A DevOps team needs to ensure that all EC2 instances and container images are regularly scanned for software vulnerabilities. They also want to ensure that any identified vulnerabilities are automatically reported to a central security dashboard for remediation tracking. Which two AWS services should be used? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon Inspector v2","AWS Security Hub","Amazon GuardDuty","AWS Config","AWS Audit Manager"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon Inspector v2) provides automated and continuous vulnerability management for EC2 instances and container images. It identifies software vulnerabilities and unintended network exposure. Option B (AWS Security Hub) aggregates security findings from various AWS services, including Amazon Inspector v2, into a single, centralized dashboard. This allows for consolidated reporting and tracking of vulnerabilities. Option C (Amazon GuardDuty) is a threat detection service, not a vulnerability scanner. Option D (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations for compliance, not software vulnerabilities. Option E (AWS Audit Manager) is for automating audit evidence collection, not for continuous vulnerability scanning or centralized security findings.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_80',
  'To establish a comprehensive security monitoring solution, an organization needs to log all API calls for auditing purposes and continuously monitor for potential threats and anomalies in their AWS environment. Which two AWS services are fundamental for this setup? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS CloudTrail","Amazon GuardDuty","AWS Config","AWS Security Hub","AWS IAM Access Analyzer"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS CloudTrail) provides event history of your AWS account activity, including actions taken through the AWS Management Console, AWS SDKs, command line tools, and other AWS services. This is crucial for auditing. Option B (Amazon GuardDuty) is a threat detection service that continuously monitors for malicious activity and unauthorized behavior to protect your AWS accounts and workloads. It analyzes CloudTrail events, VPC Flow Logs, and DNS logs to identify threats. Option C (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations for compliance, not API activity or threat detection. Option D (AWS Security Hub) aggregates findings from other services but doesn''t perform the primary logging or threat detection. Option E (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) identifies external access to resources, not general API activity logging or threat detection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  42,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_81',
  'A company wants to ensure that all resource configurations comply with internal security policies and industry standards. They also need to automatically collect evidence for compliance audits. Which two AWS services can help achieve these goals? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Config","AWS Audit Manager","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Security Hub","Amazon Macie"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Config) continuously monitors and records your AWS resource configurations, allowing you to evaluate them against desired configurations using rules and conformance packs to ensure compliance with internal security policies and industry standards. Option B (AWS Audit Manager) helps automate the collection of evidence for compliance audits, making it easier to prepare for regulatory assessments. It can integrate with AWS Config to gather configuration data. Option C (AWS CloudTrail) logs API activity, which is an input for audits but doesn''t perform compliance checks or evidence collection automation. Option D (AWS Security Hub) aggregates findings but doesn''t perform the primary configuration compliance or evidence collection. Option E (Amazon Macie) is for sensitive data discovery, not configuration compliance or audit evidence collection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_82',
  'A security team needs to identify any IAM roles or users that have not been used for an extended period, indicating potential unused access that should be revoked. They also want to ensure that any external access granted to their Amazon S3 buckets is promptly identified. Which two AWS services can assist with these tasks? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS IAM Access Analyzer","AWS Security Hub","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config","AWS Organizations"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) helps identify resources shared with an external entity and also identifies unused access for IAM roles and users, highlighting credentials that haven''t been used recently. Option B (AWS Security Hub) can ingest findings from IAM Access Analyzer, providing a centralized view of these security findings, including unused access and external access to S3 buckets, for easier management and remediation. Option C (AWS CloudTrail) logs API activity, which can be analyzed to determine usage, but Access Analyzer automates the identification of unused access. Option D (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations, not IAM access patterns or unused identities. Option E (AWS Organizations) is for managing multiple AWS accounts, not for analyzing IAM access patterns or unused access within accounts.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'medium'
);

