INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_1_68',
  'A company needs to ensure that all sensitive credentials, such as database passwords, are automatically rotated on a schedule. Additionally, they want to ensure that IAM users and roles are granted only the necessary permissions, and that any excessive permissions are identified. Which two AWS services or features can help achieve these goals? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Secrets Manager","AWS IAM Access Analyzer","AWS Lambda","AWS Organizations SCPs","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Secrets Manager) is designed for managing, retrieving, and automatically rotating secrets, including database passwords, ensuring they are kept up-to-date and secure. Option B (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) helps identify unused access for IAM roles and users, which can highlight excessive permissions that are not being utilized, thus assisting in enforcing least privilege. Option C (AWS Lambda) is often used to extend Secrets Manager''s rotation capabilities but is not the primary service for secret management itself. Option D (AWS Organizations SCPs) are for setting maximum permissions across accounts, not for analyzing specific IAM role usage within an account. Option E (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations for compliance, not specifically for identifying over-privileged IAM roles or managing secrets.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_1_69',
  'To improve the security posture of an application, a DevOps team decides to automate the rotation of all application secrets. They also need to ensure that the maximum permissions for any IAM role created by developers are restricted to a predefined set. Which two AWS services or features should they implement? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Secrets Manager","IAM Permission Boundaries","AWS Lambda","AWS Organizations SCPs","AWS IAM Access Analyzer"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Secrets Manager) is the primary service for automating the rotation of application secrets like API keys and database credentials. Option B (IAM Permission Boundaries) can be attached to IAM roles to define the maximum permissions that the role can ever have, regardless of the identity-based policies attached to it. This is effective for restricting developer-created roles. Option C (AWS Lambda) is often used with Secrets Manager for custom rotation logic but is not the core service for secret management. Option D (AWS Organizations SCPs) apply at the organizational level to all accounts, which is broader than restricting specific IAM roles within an account. Option E (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) identifies external access or unused access, not for enforcing maximum permissions for roles.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_1_70',
  'A security team wants to prevent any IAM user or role from creating resources in specific AWS regions across all accounts in their AWS Organization. They also need to ensure that database credentials are automatically rotated. Which two AWS services or features are required? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Organizations Service Control Policies (SCPs)","AWS Secrets Manager","AWS IAM Permission Boundaries","AWS Config conformance packs","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Organizations Service Control Policies - SCPs) are used to centrally manage permissions across all accounts in an AWS Organization, including restricting actions in specific AWS regions. Option B (AWS Secrets Manager) is the service designed for automatic rotation of database credentials and other secrets. Option C (AWS IAM Permission Boundaries) are used to set maximum permissions for IAM entities within a single account, not for organization-wide region restrictions. Option D (AWS Config conformance packs) are for detecting non-compliance, not preventing actions. Option E (AWS Lambda) is used to implement custom rotation logic for Secrets Manager but is not the primary service for secret management itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_1_71',
  'To enforce a strong security posture, a company needs to ensure that all IAM users are required to use Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) for console access. Additionally, they want to identify any IAM roles that have been granted permissions but have never been used. Which two AWS services or features can help achieve these? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)","AWS IAM Access Analyzer","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Organizations SCPs","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Multi-Factor Authentication - MFA) is a security feature that requires users to provide two or more verification factors to gain access to a resource, directly addressing the requirement for enhanced console access security. Option B (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) helps identify unused access for IAM roles and users, highlighting roles that have permissions but no recent activity. Option C (AWS CloudTrail) logs API activity, which can be analyzed for MFA usage or role activity, but Access Analyzer automates the identification of unused access. Option D (AWS Organizations SCPs) can enforce MFA across accounts, but MFA itself is the feature. SCPs are not for identifying unused roles. Option E (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations, not MFA enforcement or unused IAM roles.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_1_72',
  'A DevOps team is implementing a new application that requires access to several external APIs. They need to securely store the API keys and ensure they are automatically rotated. They also want to ensure that the application''s IAM role has only the minimum necessary permissions. Which two AWS services or features should they use? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Secrets Manager","IAM Policies","AWS Lambda","AWS IAM Access Analyzer","AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Secrets Manager) is the service for securely storing and automatically rotating API keys and other secrets. Option B (IAM Policies) are used to define the specific permissions granted to an IAM role, allowing the team to implement the principle of least privilege by granting only the minimum necessary permissions for the application. Option C (AWS Lambda) is often used with Secrets Manager for custom rotation logic but is not the primary service for secret storage or policy definition. Option D (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) helps identify unused access or external access, which is a detective control, not for defining the initial least privilege. Option E (AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store) can store secrets but does not offer automated rotation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  67,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_1_73',
