  'multiple',
  '["AWS Secrets Manager","AWS Organizations Service Control Policies (SCPs)","AWS Lambda","IAM Permission Boundaries","AWS IAM Access Analyzer"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Secrets Manager) is specifically designed for managing, retrieving, and automatically rotating database credentials for services like Amazon RDS. Option B (AWS Organizations Service Control Policies - SCPs) can be used at the organizational level to prevent any account from creating IAM roles with administrative privileges, acting as a preventive guardrail. Option C (AWS Lambda) is often used with Secrets Manager for custom rotation logic but is not the primary service for secret management or policy enforcement. Option D (IAM Permission Boundaries) can restrict permissions for roles within an account, but SCPs are more effective for preventing administrative privileges across an entire organization. Option E (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) identifies external access or unused access, not for enforcing preventive controls on role creation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  68,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_1',
  'medium'
);

