VALUES (
  'q_40_m_40_2_106',
  'An organization wants to automatically enforce a security policy that all Amazon S3 buckets must have public access blocked. Order the steps to implement an automated remediation process using AWS Config with the LEAST manual effort.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS Config rule to detect non-compliant Amazon S3 buckets.","Enable AWS Config recording for S3 buckets.","Associate an AWS Systems Manager Automation document with the Config rule for remediation.","Deploy the AWS Config rule and enable auto-remediation."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To implement automated remediation for S3 public access, first, AWS Config recording must be enabled for S3 buckets (Option B) to track their configuration changes. Next, an AWS Config rule is created (Option A) to evaluate S3 bucket compliance against the public access policy. Then, an AWS Systems Manager Automation document is associated with this Config rule (Option C) to define the remediation steps. Finally, the Config rule is deployed and auto-remediation is enabled (Option D) to automatically fix non-compliant buckets.',
