  'To enable Amazon GuardDuty, you first enable the service in your AWS account, which starts monitoring immediately (Option B). Next, you can configure optional trusted IP lists or threat lists to fine-tune GuardDuty''s detection capabilities (Option C). Then, you review the generated security findings in the GuardDuty console to understand potential threats (Option A). Finally, for automated response, you can integrate GuardDuty findings with Amazon EventBridge to trigger AWS Lambda functions or other actions (Option D).',
