  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Before using SCPs, AWS Organizations must be configured with all features enabled (Option B). Next, you create a new Service Control Policy (SCP) with the specific permissions you want to enforce or deny (Option C). After creating the SCP, you attach it to the target Organizational Unit (OU) or directly to accounts (Option A). Finally, it is crucial to test the SCP''s effect on member accounts within the OU to ensure it behaves as expected and doesn''t inadvertently block necessary actions (Option D).',
