  '{2,0,3,1}',
  'To set up continuous vulnerability scanning with Amazon Inspector v2, the first step is to enable Amazon Inspector in the desired AWS account and Region (Option C). Amazon Inspector leverages the AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent), so you must ensure the SSM Agent is installed on your EC2 instances (Option A) for Inspector to collect data. Next, configure scanning preferences, such as instance tags or exclusions (Option D), to define the scope of your scans. Finally, review the generated vulnerability findings in the Amazon Inspector console (Option B) to identify and address security issues.',
