INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_104',
  'A financial institution is preparing for an upcoming regulatory audit and needs to automate the collection of evidence to demonstrate compliance with specific controls. The audit team wants to streamline the evidence gathering process. Order the steps to effectively use AWS Audit Manager for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define an assessment in AWS Audit Manager, selecting a pre-built framework or creating a custom one.","Configure the data sources for the assessment, such as AWS services (e.g., CloudTrail, Config) and AWS Security Hub.","Initiate the evidence collection process and allow Audit Manager to gather relevant data.","Generate an audit report from the collected evidence, which can be shared with auditors."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To automate evidence collection with AWS Audit Manager, first define an assessment (Option A) by selecting a suitable pre-built framework or creating a custom one tailored to the audit requirements. Next, configure the data sources (Option B) for this assessment, specifying which AWS services (like CloudTrail or Config) and Security Hub findings Audit Manager should collect evidence from. Then, initiate the evidence collection process (Option C), allowing Audit Manager to automatically gather and organize the relevant data. Finally, generate an audit report (Option D) from the collected evidence, which provides a comprehensive, structured document for auditors.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_105',
  'A DevOps team is adopting Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using AWS CloudFormation and needs to enforce strict security and compliance policies on their templates before deployment. They want to prevent non-compliant infrastructure from being provisioned. Order the steps to integrate CloudFormation Guard for policy-as-code enforcement in their CI/CD pipeline.',
  'ordering',
  '["Develop CloudFormation templates for infrastructure provisioning.","Write CloudFormation Guard rules that define the required security and compliance policies.","Integrate a Guard scan step into the CI/CD pipeline to evaluate templates against the rules.","Configure the pipeline to block deployments if CloudFormation Guard identifies any policy violations."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To integrate CloudFormation Guard for policy-as-code enforcement, first develop the CloudFormation templates (Option A) that define the infrastructure. Next, write CloudFormation Guard rules (Option B) that specify the security and compliance policies these templates must adhere to. Then, integrate a Guard scan step (Option C) into the CI/CD pipeline, which will evaluate the templates against the defined rules. Finally, configure the pipeline to block deployments (Option D) if CloudFormation Guard detects any policy violations, ensuring only compliant infrastructure is provisioned.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_106',
  'A company handles sensitive customer data stored in Amazon S3 buckets and needs to identify, classify, and protect this data to meet regulatory requirements. The security team wants to automate the discovery of Personally Identifiable Information (PII). Order the steps to effectively use Amazon Macie for data classification and protection.',
  'ordering',
  '["Enable Amazon Macie across the AWS accounts and regions where S3 buckets are located.","Define custom sensitive data types in Macie, if needed, to identify specific proprietary information.","Configure Macie to run discovery jobs on target S3 buckets or prefixes.","Review the findings generated by Macie to understand sensitive data exposure and prioritize remediation actions."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To use Amazon Macie for data classification, first enable Amazon Macie (Option A) in the relevant AWS accounts and regions. Next, define custom sensitive data types (Option B) in Macie if there''s proprietary information beyond Macie''s built-in detectors that needs to be identified. Then, configure Macie to run discovery jobs (Option C) on the specific S3 buckets or prefixes that contain sensitive data. Finally, review the findings (Option D) generated by Macie to gain insights into sensitive data exposure and prioritize necessary remediation actions to protect the data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_107',
  'A security operations center (SOC) needs to establish continuous threat detection for an AWS environment to identify malicious activity and unauthorized behavior. The team wants to leverage Amazon GuardDuty for this purpose and integrate its findings into their existing security workflows. Order the steps to set up and utilize Amazon GuardDuty.',
  'ordering',
  '["Enable Amazon GuardDuty in all relevant AWS accounts and regions.","Configure trusted IP lists and threat lists within GuardDuty to refine detection.","Review the findings generated by GuardDuty in the console or via integration with AWS Security Hub.","Integrate GuardDuty findings with an incident response system or SIEM for automated alerts and actions."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To set up Amazon GuardDuty, the first step is to enable the service (Option A) in all relevant AWS accounts and regions to begin monitoring. Next, configure trusted IP lists and threat lists (Option B) within GuardDuty to enhance detection accuracy and reduce false positives. Then, review the findings (Option C) generated by GuardDuty, either directly in the console or through integration with AWS Security Hub for a centralized view. Finally, integrate GuardDuty findings (Option D) with an incident response system or SIEM to enable automated alerts and facilitate prompt action on detected threats.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_108',
  'A company needs to ensure that all data stored in its Amazon RDS PostgreSQL databases is encrypted at rest using customer-managed keys for enhanced security and compliance. Order the steps to implement data encryption at rest for an Amazon RDS instance using AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS).',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new customer managed key (CMK) in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS).","Configure the Amazon RDS instance to use the newly created KMS key for encryption at rest.","Migrate existing unencrypted databases to new encrypted instances, or ensure new instances are created with encryption enabled.","Monitor the usage of the KMS key and audit access to ensure compliance with security policies."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To implement data encryption at rest for RDS with KMS, first create a new customer managed key (CMK) in AWS KMS (Option A), which provides granular control over the encryption key. Next, configure the Amazon RDS instance (Option B) to utilize this KMS key for encryption at rest during creation or modification. Then, migrate any existing unencrypted databases (Option C) to new encrypted instances, or ensure all new databases are provisioned with encryption enabled. Finally, monitor the usage of the KMS key (Option D) and audit access to it, ensuring compliance and maintaining control over the encryption process.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  42,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_109',
  'A security team needs to create a custom AWS Config rule to monitor a specific, non-standard configuration requirement for Amazon EC2 instances that is not covered by existing managed rules. This rule should automatically check for compliance. Order the steps to implement a custom AWS Config rule using an AWS Lambda function.',
  'ordering',
  '["Develop an AWS Lambda function that contains the logic to evaluate the compliance of EC2 instances against the custom requirement.","Create a new custom AWS Config rule and associate it with the Lambda function and the target EC2 resource type.","Configure the AWS Config rule to trigger evaluations periodically or based on configuration changes.","Monitor the compliance status of EC2 instances in the AWS Config console and address any non-compliant resources."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To implement a custom AWS Config rule, first develop an AWS Lambda function (Option A) that encapsulates the custom logic for evaluating EC2 instance compliance. Next, create a new custom AWS Config rule (Option B) and link it to this Lambda function, specifying Amazon EC2 as the target resource type. Then, configure the AWS Config rule (Option C) to trigger evaluations either periodically or in response to configuration changes. Finally, monitor the compliance status (Option D) of EC2 instances in the AWS Config console and initiate remediation for any non-compliant resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain41_8',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_41_3',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_41_m_41_3_110',
  'A company needs to generate an audit report for a specific compliance standard (e.g., PCI DSS) by collecting evidence from various AWS services. The audit team wants to automate this process to reduce manual effort and ensure accuracy. Order the steps to automate audit evidence collection and reporting using AWS Audit Manager.',
  'ordering',
